{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133002364,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1baa90708002ItYJL6szFiW5Qa","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baa902a20014J5wmzOFe1ibcg","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8be88707a2f055c0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":260,"offset":2142,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 2142-2401\n2142:   phase_synthesis:\n2143:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into final research/research.md\n2144:     steps:\n2145: \n2146:       step_fanout_merge:\n2147:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries into one consolidated registry; skip when single-executor\"\n2148:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n2149:         command: |\n2150:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n2151:             --loop-type research \\\n2152:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n2153:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2154:         wait_for_completion: true\n2155: \n2156:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n2157:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n2158:         read:\n2159:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2160:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2161:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n2162:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2163:         read_patterns:\n2164:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n2165:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-research-strategy.md\"\n2166:         extract:\n2167:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count type === 'iteration' across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n2168:           - current_iteration: \"iteration_count + 1\"\n2169:           - current_segment: \"Latest segment_start event segment, else 1\"\n2170:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n2171:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newInfoRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n2172:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newInfoRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n2173:           - remaining_questions: \"Count unchecked items in 'Key Questions'\"\n2174:           - remaining_questions_list: \"List unchecked key questions from strategy.md\"\n2175:           - answered_count: \"Count answered questions from strategy.md\"\n2176:           - total_questions: \"Count total questions tracked in strategy.md\"\n2177:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: focus (ratio)'\"\n2178:           - divergence_summary: \"Read registry.divergence and summarize saturated directions, completed pivots, failures, overrides, Council artifact refs, and remaining frontier; else 'no divergent pivots recorded'\"\n2179:           - reason: \"Use the latest synthesis/recovery stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n2180: \n2181:       step_read_all_iterations:\n2182:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n2183:         read_patterns:\n2184:           - \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n2185:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/iterations/iteration-*.md\"\n2186:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2187:         identity: \"Preserve each full source path and lineage label. Duplicate basenames from different lineages are distinct synthesis inputs; do not copy or renumber them.\"\n2188:         selection: \"When lineage iteration files exist, synthesize from those files in stable lineage-plus-iteration order; otherwise use root iterations.\"\n2189: \n2190:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2191:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged research deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2192:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n2193:         if_present:\n2194:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} --emit-resource-map --fanout-resource-map-only\"\n2195:           read:\n2196:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2197:             - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2198:             - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deltas/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2199:         if_absent:\n2200:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} --emit-resource-map\"\n2201:           read:\n2202:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2203:             - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2204:         write:\n2205:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2206:         guarantee: \"Fan-out resource-map emission reads lineage deltas in place and writes only resource-map.md; it never rewrites merged registries, strategy, or dashboard. Single-executor reduction remains unchanged.\"\n2207: \n2208:       step_compile_research:\n2209:         action: \"Compile or finalize research/research.md\"\n2210:         instructions: |\n2211:           If research/research.md exists (progressive synthesis was active):\n2212:             1. Read current research/research.md\n2213:             2. Consolidate and deduplicate findings across all iterations\n2214:             3. Fill any empty sections with findings from iteration files\n2215:             4. Remove redundancy while preserving all unique findings\n2216:             5. Add convergence report as appendix\n2217:             6. If `resource_map_present` is true, cite `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` in References; otherwise omit any placeholder map citation\n2218:             7. Preserve the mandatory `## Eliminated Alternatives` section, then add or replace `## Divergence Map` immediately after it and before Section 12 Open Questions. Populate it from `{state_paths.registry}` with saturated directions, pivots taken, evidence and Council artifact references, pivot failures and audited overrides, and the remaining frontier.\n2219: \n2220:           If research/research.md does not exist:\n2221:             1. Create research/research.md following 17-section template\n2222:             2. Populate sections from iteration files\n2223:             3. Add citations from original sources\n2224:             4. Note unanswered questions in Open Questions section\n2225:             5. If `resource_map_present` is true, cite `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` in References; otherwise omit any placeholder map citation\n2226:             6. After the mandatory `## Eliminated Alternatives` section and before Section 12 Open Questions, add `## Divergence Map` with saturated directions, pivots taken, evidence and Council artifact references, pivot failures and audited overrides, and the remaining frontier from `{state_paths.registry}`.\n2227:           Divergence Map documents breadth. Never claim the topic converged merely because divergent mode broadened the investigated frontier.\n2228:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branch Contract`.)\n2229:         output: \"{state_paths.research_output}\"\n2230: \n2231:       step_convergence_report:\n2232:         action: \"Generate and append convergence report\"\n2233:         report: |\n2234:           ## Convergence Report\n2235:           - Stop reason: {reason}\n2236:           - Total iterations: {iteration_count}\n2237:           - Questions answered: {answered_count} / {total_questions}\n2238:           - Remaining questions: {remaining_questions}\n2239:           - Last 3 iteration summaries: {last_3_summaries}\n2240:           - Convergence threshold: {convergence_threshold}\n2241:           - Divergence summary: {divergence_summary}\n2242:           - Segment transitions, wave scores, and checkpoint metrics are experimental and omitted from the live report.\n2243:         command: |\n2244:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2245:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2246:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-research-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2247:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2248:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2249:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode research --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2250:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2251:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2252:             --registry \"{state_paths.registry}\" \\\n2253:             --output \"{state_paths.research_output}\" \\\n2254:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2255:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2256:             --answered-count \"{answered_count}\" --total-questions \"{total_questions}\"\n2257:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2258:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2259:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2260:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode research --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2261:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2262:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2263:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2264:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2265:             fi\n2266:           done\n2267:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2268:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2269: \n2270:       step_writeback_spec_findings:\n2271:         action: \"Write or replace the bounded generated findings block in spec.md before config completion\"\n2272:         edit: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n2273:         host_anchor: \"Use the chosen host anchor required by spec_check_protocol\"\n2274:         generated_fence_begin: \"<!-- BEGIN GENERATED: deep-research/spec-findings -->\"\n2275:         generated_fence_end: \"<!-- END GENERATED: deep-research/spec-findings -->\"\n2276:         fail_closed_conflict_check:\n2277:           if_existing_generated_fence_present:\n2278:             detect_manual_edits: \"Use generated checksum metadata or an explicit MANUAL-EDIT marker inside the existing fence to detect human edits before overwrite.\"\n2279:             on_manual_edit_conflict:\n2280:               append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation_conflict\",\"folder_state\":\"conflict-detected\",\"reason\":\"Manual edits detected inside existing generated findings fence.\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"generatedFence\":\"deep-research/spec-findings\",\"conflictKind\":\"generated-fence-manual-edit\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2281:               halt: true\n2282:         instructions:\n2283:           - \"Read `{state_paths.research_output}` as the canonical synthesis source.\"\n2284:           - \"Replace exactly one generated findings block under the chosen host anchor.\"\n2285:           - \"Fail closed if the host anchor is missing, duplicate markers exist, or human edits are detected inside the generated block.\"\n2286:           - \"Do not overwrite a generated block that fails checksum validation or carries an explicit MANUAL-EDIT marker.\"\n2287:           - \"Emit `spec_synthesis_deferred` instead of partial output when synthesis cannot safely write back.\"\n2288:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation\",\"phase\":\"post-synthesis\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"<chosen host anchor>\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Replaced generated deep-research findings fence from research/research.md.\",\"generatedFence\":\"deep-research/spec-findings\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2289: \n2290:       step_validate_post_synthesis_spec_doc:\n2291:         action: \"Run targeted strict validation after deep-research writes back into spec.md\"\n2292:         command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n2293:         note: \"Fail closed before completion if the deep-research spec.md sync breaks the authored-spec structural contract. This targeted check uses the fast Node validation orchestrator.\"\n2294: \n2295:       step_update_config_status:\n2296:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2297:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2298:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2299: \n2300:       step_telemetry_heartbeat_terminal:\n2301:         action: \"Emit a single-loop terminal row in the orchestration status ledger\"\n2302:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2303:         terminal_events: [completed, failed, stopped]\n2304:         command: |\n2305:           node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n2306:           import { existsSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n2307: \n2308:           import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n2309:           import observabilityEvents from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n2310: \n2311:           const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n2312:           const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n2313:           const config = JSON.parse(readFileSync('{state_paths.config}', 'utf8'));\n2314:           const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n2315:           const sessionId = String(config.lineage?.sessionId ?? '{config.lineage.sessionId}');\n2316:           const generation = Number(config.lineage?.generation ?? '{config.lineage.generation}');\n2317:           const reason = '{reason}';\n2318:           const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n2319: \n2320:           function readRecords(path) {\n2321:             if (!existsSync(path)) return [];\n2322:             return readFileSync(path, 'utf8')\n2323:               .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n2324:               .map((line) => line.trim())\n2325:               .filter(Boolean)\n2326:               .map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n2327:           }\n2328: \n2329:           function elapsedSince(value) {\n2330:             const startedAtMs = Date.parse(String(value ?? ''));\n2331:             const nowMs = Date.parse(timestamp);\n2332:             if (!Number.isFinite(startedAtMs) || !Number.isFinite(nowMs)) return 0;\n2333:             return Math.max(0, nowMs - startedAtMs);\n2334:           }\n2335: \n2336:           function terminalEvent(stopReason) {\n2337:             if (stopReason === 'manualStop' || stopReason === 'userPaused') return 'stopped';\n2338:             if (stopReason === 'error') return 'failed';\n2339:             return 'completed';\n2340:           }\n2341: \n2342:           const records = readRecords(stateLogPath);\n2343:           const iterations = records.filter((record) => record.type === 'iteration');\n2344:           const latest = iterations.at(-1) ?? {};\n2345:           const startedAt = records.find((record) => typeof record.createdAt === 'string')?.createdAt\n2346:             ?? records.find((record) => typeof record.timestamp === 'string')?.timestamp\n2347:             ?? timestamp;\n2348:           const elapsedMs = elapsedSince(startedAt);\n2349:           const score = Number.isFinite(Number(latest.newInfoRatio)) ? Number(latest.newInfoRatio) : 0;\n2350:           const event = terminalEvent(reason);\n2351:           const row = {\n2352:             event,\n2353:             label: 'single',\n2354:             terminal: true,\n2355:             reason,\n2356:             at: timestamp,\n2357:             duration_ms: elapsedMs,\n2358:             loop_type: 'research',\n2359:             sessionId,\n2360:             generation,\n2361:             gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, elapsed_ms: elapsedMs, score },\n2362:           };\n2363: \n2364:           const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n2365:             diffData: { event, label: row.label, reason, sessionId, generation, gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, score } },\n2366:             diffField: 'state_hash',\n2367:           });\n2368:           if (appended) {\n2369:             try {\n2370:               appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n2371:                 producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n2372:                 stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n2373:                 subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation, reason },\n2374:                 event,\n2375:                 status: event,\n2376:               });\n2377:             } catch {}\n2378:           }\n2379:           EOF\n2380:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2381:         outputs:\n2382:           - status_ledger_terminal: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event completed, failed, or stopped\"\n2383: \n2384:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2385:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2386:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2387:         command: 'git add -- \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research.lock\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research-pause\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research-run-now\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.legacy-projection-watermarks\"'\n2388:         note: \"Skill-owned contract fix (028): without this stage step, operators who do `git add research-report.md` lose the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, etc.). Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the audit trail intact. Operators retain commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` to unstage anything before commit. Failure is non-fatal: log warning and continue. The exclude pathspecs keep the live lock file, the pause and run-now sentinels, and the legacy projection watermark directory out of the index; locks-and-fencing-v1, ledgers, deltas, iterations and the state log stay staged.\"\n2389:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2390: \n2391:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2392:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2393:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2394:   phase_save:\n2395:     purpose: Preserve research context in the packet's canonical continuity documents\n2396:     steps:\n2397: \n2398:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2399:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2400:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2401:         requirements:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2402]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 2142-2401\n2142:   phase_synthesis:\n2143:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into final research/research.md\n2144:     steps:\n2145: \n2146:       step_fanout_merge:\n2147:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries into one consolidated registry; skip when single-executor\"\n2148:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n2149:         command: |\n2150:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n2151:             --loop-type research \\\n2152:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n2153:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2154:         wait_for_completion: true\n2155: \n2156:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n2157:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n2158:         read:\n2159:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2160:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2161:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n2162:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2163:         read_patterns:\n2164:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n2165:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-research-strategy.md\"\n2166:         extract:\n2167:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count type === 'iteration' across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n2168:           - current_iteration: \"iteration_count + 1\"\n2169:           - current_segment: \"Latest segment_start event segment, else 1\"\n2170:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n2171:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newInfoRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n2172:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newInfoRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n2173:           - remaining_questions: \"Count unchecked items in 'Key Questions'\"\n2174:           - remaining_questions_list: \"List unchecked key questions from strategy.md\"\n2175:           - answered_count: \"Count answered questions from strategy.md\"\n2176:           - total_questions: \"Count total questions tracked in strategy.md\"\n2177:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: focus (ratio)'\"\n2178:           - divergence_summary: \"Read registry.divergence and summarize saturated directions, completed pivots, failures, overrides, Council artifact refs, and remaining frontier; else 'no divergent pivots recorded'\"\n2179:           - reason: \"Use the latest synthesis/recovery stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n2180: \n2181:       step_read_all_iterations:\n2182:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n2183:         read_patterns:\n2184:           - \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n2185:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/iterations/iteration-*.md\"\n2186:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2187:         identity: \"Preserve each full source path and lineage label. Duplicate basenames from different lineages are distinct synthesis inputs; do not copy or renumber them.\"\n2188:         selection: \"When lineage iteration files exist, synthesize from those files in stable lineage-plus-iteration order; otherwise use root iterations.\"\n2189: \n2190:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2191:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged research deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2192:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n2193:         if_present:\n2194:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} --emit-resource-map --fanout-resource-map-only\"\n2195:           read:\n2196:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2197:             - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2198:             - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deltas/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2199:         if_absent:\n2200:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} --emit-resource-map\"\n2201:           read:\n2202:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2203:             - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2204:         write:\n2205:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2206:         guarantee: \"Fan-out resource-map emission reads lineage deltas in place and writes only resource-map.md; it never rewrites merged registries, strategy, or dashboard. Single-executor reduction remains unchanged.\"\n2207: \n2208:       step_compile_research:\n2209:         action: \"Compile or finalize research/research.md\"\n2210:         instructions: |\n2211:           If research/research.md exists (progressive synthesis was active):\n2212:             1. Read current research/research.md\n2213:             2. Consolidate and deduplicate findings across all iterations\n2214:             3. Fill any empty sections with findings from iteration files\n2215:             4. Remove redundancy while preserving all unique findings\n2216:             5. Add convergence report as appendix\n2217:             6. If `resource_map_present` is true, cite `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` in References; otherwise omit any placeholder map citation\n2218:             7. Preserve the mandatory `## Eliminated Alternatives` section, then add or replace `## Divergence Map` immediately after it and before Section 12 Open Questions. Populate it from `{state_paths.registry}` with saturated directions, pivots taken, evidence and Council artifact references, pivot failures and audited overrides, and the remaining frontier.\n2219: \n2220:           If research/research.md does not exist:\n2221:             1. Create research/research.md following 17-section template\n2222:             2. Populate sections from iteration files\n2223:             3. Add citations from original sources\n2224:             4. Note unanswered questions in Open Questions section\n2225:             5. If `resource_map_present` is true, cite `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` in References; otherwise omit any placeholder map citation\n2226:             6. After the mandatory `## Eliminated Alternatives` section and before Section 12 Open Questions, add `## Divergence Map` with saturated directions, pivots taken, evidence and Council artifact references, pivot failures and audited overrides, and the remaining frontier from `{state_paths.registry}`.\n2227:           Divergence Map documents breadth. Never claim the topic converged merely because divergent mode broadened the investigated frontier.\n2228:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branch Contract`.)\n2229:         output: \"{state_paths.research_output}\"\n2230: \n2231:       step_convergence_report:\n2232:         action: \"Generate and append convergence report\"\n2233:         report: |\n2234:           ## Convergence Report\n2235:           - Stop reason: {reason}\n2236:           - Total iterations: {iteration_count}\n2237:           - Questions answered: {answered_count} / {total_questions}\n2238:           - Remaining questions: {remaining_questions}\n2239:           - Last 3 iteration summaries: {last_3_summaries}\n2240:           - Convergence threshold: {convergence_threshold}\n2241:           - Divergence summary: {divergence_summary}\n2242:           - Segment transitions, wave scores, and checkpoint metrics are experimental and omitted from the live report.\n2243:         command: |\n2244:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2245:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2246:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-research-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2247:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2248:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2249:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode research --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2250:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2251:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2252:             --registry \"{state_paths.registry}\" \\\n2253:             --output \"{state_paths.research_output}\" \\\n2254:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2255:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2256:             --answered-count \"{answered_count}\" --total-questions \"{total_questions}\"\n2257:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2258:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2259:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2260:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode research --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2261:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2262:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2263:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2264:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2265:             fi\n2266:           done\n2267:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2268:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2269: \n2270:       step_writeback_spec_findings:\n2271:         action: \"Write or replace the bounded generated findings block in spec.md before config completion\"\n2272:         edit: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n2273:         host_anchor: \"Use the chosen host anchor required by spec_check_protocol\"\n2274:         generated_fence_begin: \"<!-- BEGIN GENERATED: deep-research/spec-findings -->\"\n2275:         generated_fence_end: \"<!-- END GENERATED: deep-research/spec-findings -->\"\n2276:         fail_closed_conflict_check:\n2277:           if_existing_generated_fence_present:\n2278:             detect_manual_edits: \"Use generated checksum metadata or an explicit MANUAL-EDIT marker inside the existing fence to detect human edits before overwrite.\"\n2279:             on_manual_edit_conflict:\n2280:               append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation_conflict\",\"folder_state\":\"conflict-detected\",\"reason\":\"Manual edits detected inside existing generated findings fence.\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"generatedFence\":\"deep-research/spec-findings\",\"conflictKind\":\"generated-fence-manual-edit\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2281:               halt: true\n2282:         instructions:\n2283:           - \"Read `{state_paths.research_output}` as the canonical synthesis source.\"\n2284:           - \"Replace exactly one generated findings block under the chosen host anchor.\"\n2285:           - \"Fail closed if the host anchor is missing, duplicate markers exist, or human edits are detected inside the generated block.\"\n2286:           - \"Do not overwrite a generated block that fails checksum validation or carries an explicit MANUAL-EDIT marker.\"\n2287:           - \"Emit `spec_synthesis_deferred` instead of partial output when synthesis cannot safely write back.\"\n2288:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation\",\"phase\":\"post-synthesis\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"<chosen host anchor>\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Replaced generated deep-research findings fence from research/research.md.\",\"generatedFence\":\"deep-research/spec-findings\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2289: \n2290:       step_validate_post_synthesis_spec_doc:\n2291:         action: \"Run targeted strict validation after deep-research writes back into spec.md\"\n2292:         command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n2293:         note: \"Fail closed before completion if the deep-research spec.md sync breaks the authored-spec structural contract. This targeted check uses the fast Node validation orchestrator.\"\n2294: \n2295:       step_update_config_status:\n2296:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2297:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2298:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2299: \n2300:       step_telemetry_heartbeat_terminal:\n2301:         action: \"Emit a single-loop terminal row in the orchestration status ledger\"\n2302:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2303:         terminal_events: [completed, failed, stopped]\n2304:         command: |\n2305:           node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n2306:           import { existsSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n2307: \n2308:           import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n2309:           import observabilityEvents from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n2310: \n2311:           const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n2312:           const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n2313:           const config = JSON.parse(readFileSync('{state_paths.config}', 'utf8'));\n2314:           const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n2315:           const sessionId = String(config.lineage?.sessionId ?? '{config.lineage.sessionId}');\n2316:           const generation = Number(config.lineage?.generation ?? '{config.lineage.generation}');\n2317:           const reason = '{reason}';\n2318:           const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n2319: \n2320:           function readRecords(path) {\n2321:             if (!existsSync(path)) return [];\n2322:             return readFileSync(path, 'utf8')\n2323:               .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n2324:               .map((line) => line.trim())\n2325:               .filter(Boolean)\n2326:               .map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n2327:           }\n2328: \n2329:           function elapsedSince(value) {\n2330:             const startedAtMs = Date.parse(String(value ?? ''));\n2331:             const nowMs = Date.parse(timestamp);\n2332:             if (!Number.isFinite(startedAtMs) || !Number.isFinite(nowMs)) return 0;\n2333:             return Math.max(0, nowMs - startedAtMs);\n2334:           }\n2335: \n2336:           function terminalEvent(stopReason) {\n2337:             if (stopReason === 'manualStop' || stopReason === 'userPaused') return 'stopped';\n2338:             if (stopReason === 'error') return 'failed';\n2339:             return 'completed';\n2340:           }\n2341: \n2342:           const records = readRecords(stateLogPath);\n2343:           const iterations = records.filter((record) => record.type === 'iteration');\n2344:           const latest = iterations.at(-1) ?? {};\n2345:           const startedAt = records.find((record) => typeof record.createdAt === 'string')?.createdAt\n2346:             ?? records.find((record) => typeof record.timestamp === 'string')?.timestamp\n2347:             ?? timestamp;\n2348:           const elapsedMs = elapsedSince(startedAt);\n2349:           const score = Number.isFinite(Number(latest.newInfoRatio)) ? Number(latest.newInfoRatio) : 0;\n2350:           const event = terminalEvent(reason);\n2351:           const row = {\n2352:             event,\n2353:             label: 'single',\n2354:             terminal: true,\n2355:             reason,\n2356:             at: timestamp,\n2357:             duration_ms: elapsedMs,\n2358:             loop_type: 'research',\n2359:             sessionId,\n2360:             generation,\n2361:             gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, elapsed_ms: elapsedMs, score },\n2362:           };\n2363: \n2364:           const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n2365:             diffData: { event, label: row.label, reason, sessionId, generation, gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, score } },\n2366:             diffField: 'state_hash',\n2367:           });\n2368:           if (appended) {\n2369:             try {\n2370:               appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n2371:                 producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n2372:                 stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n2373:                 subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation, reason },\n2374:                 event,\n2375:                 status: event,\n2376:               });\n2377:             } catch {}\n2378:           }\n2379:           EOF\n2380:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2381:         outputs:\n2382:           - status_ledger_terminal: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event completed, failed, or stopped\"\n2383: \n2384:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2385:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2386:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2387:         command: 'git add -- \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research.lock\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research-pause\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research-run-now\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.legacy-projection-watermarks\"'\n2388:         note: \"Skill-owned contract fix (028): without this stage step, operators who do `git add research-report.md` lose the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, etc.). Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the audit trail intact. Operators retain commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` to unstage anything before commit. Failure is non-fatal: log warning and continue. The exclude pathspecs keep the live lock file, the pause and run-now sentinels, and the legacy projection watermark directory out of the index; locks-and-fencing-v1, ledgers, deltas, iterations and the state log stay staged.\"\n2389:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2390: \n2391:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2392:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2393:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2394:   phase_save:\n2395:     purpose: Preserve research context in the packet's canonical continuity documents\n2396:     steps:\n2397: \n2398:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2399:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2400:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2401:         requirements:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2402]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 260, \"offset\": 2142, \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133001992,"end":1794133002364}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794133003175,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"id":"prt_1baa90ba7001bbRHIGGYJcpxu7","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baa902a20014J5wmzOFe1ibcg","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"b17639a35508c05f52ebd0e190239ccd250b29aa","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":5782,"output":84,"reasoning":14,"cache":{"read":47488,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794133004158,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"id":"prt_1baa90f7e001gGqbJyfB5wwX5G","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baa90bab001SmUnYq7B2KKCGY","type":"step-start","snapshot":"b17639a35508c05f52ebd0e190239ccd250b29aa"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133007233,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1baa91a4a001HhuueUqnyAtn98","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baa90bab001SmUnYq7B2KKCGY","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2ef16e0f9aad2ff","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md, lines 1-188\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research strategy\"\n6:   - \"research strategy template\"\n7:   - \"research session tracking\"\n8:   - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n9:   - \"research stop conditions\"\n10:   - \"ruled out research directions\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: planning\n13: version: 1.14.0.19\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n17: \n18: Runtime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n29: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n30: - **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n31: - **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n32: \n33: ### Question Injection Surface\n34: \n35: Use `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n36: \n37: - `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n38: - `text`: question text to promote\n39: - `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n40: - `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n41: - `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n42: - `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n43: \n44: The reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n45: \n46: Question ownership is explicit:\n47: \n48: - Inbox rows are immutable input.\n49: - The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n50: - Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n51: \n52: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 2. TOPIC\n57: [Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n62: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n63: Generated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n64: \n65: - [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n66: - [ ] [Question 2]\n67: - [ ] [Question 3]\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n73: [What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n78: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n83: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n84: [None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n91: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n92: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n93: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n99: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n100: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n101: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n108: [Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n109: \n110: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n111: - What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n112: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n113: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n114: \n115: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n116: - What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n117: - Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n123: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n124: [Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n125: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n131: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n132: - Completed pivots: 0\n133: - Failed pivots: 0\n134: - Audited overrides: 0\n135: - Saturated: none yet\n136: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n137: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n143: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n144: [Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n145: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n157: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n159: \n160: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n161: \n162: Populate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n163: \n164: - Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n165: - Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n166: - Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n167: - Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n168: \n169: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n174: - Max iterations: [from config]\n175: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n176: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n177: - Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n178: - research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n179: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n180: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n181: - Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n182: - Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n183: - Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n184: - Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n185: - Capability matrix doc: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n186: - Capability resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n187: - Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n188: - Started: [timestamp]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md, lines 1-188\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research strategy\"\n6:   - \"research strategy template\"\n7:   - \"research session tracking\"\n8:   - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n9:   - \"research stop conditions\"\n10:   - \"ruled out research directions\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: planning\n13: version: 1.14.0.19\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n17: \n18: Runtime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n29: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n30: - **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n31: - **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n32: \n33: ### Question Injection Surface\n34: \n35: Use `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n36: \n37: - `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n38: - `text`: question text to promote\n39: - `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n40: - `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n41: - `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n42: - `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n43: \n44: The reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n45: \n46: Question ownership is explicit:\n47: \n48: - Inbox rows are immutable input.\n49: - The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n50: - Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n51: \n52: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 2. TOPIC\n57: [Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n62: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n63: Generated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n64: \n65: - [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n66: - [ ] [Question 2]\n67: - [ ] [Question 3]\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n73: [What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n78: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n83: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n84: [None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n91: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n92: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n93: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n99: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n100: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n101: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n108: [Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n109: \n110: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n111: - What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n112: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n113: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n114: \n115: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n116: - What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n117: - Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n123: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n124: [Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n125: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n131: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n132: - Completed pivots: 0\n133: - Failed pivots: 0\n134: - Audited overrides: 0\n135: - Saturated: none yet\n136: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n137: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n143: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n144: [Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n145: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n157: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n159: \n160: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n161: \n162: Populate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n163: \n164: - Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n165: - Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n166: - Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n167: - Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n168: \n169: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n174: - Max iterations: [from config]\n175: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n176: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n177: - Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n178: - research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n179: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n180: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n181: - Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n182: - Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n183: - Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n184: - Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n185: - Capability matrix doc: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n186: - Capability resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n187: - Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n188: - Started: [timestamp]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133006922,"end":1794133007233}}}}
