{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133079088,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1baaa31ef0021vE1UCP4lpuX0l","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baaa293c001V3qnPayb7zZ3ov","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf8f6b50cd3a2bc0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/fanout.json; echo \"---\"; cat specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/topic.txt | head -30; echo \"---\"; ls specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/"},"output":"{\"concurrency\":1,\"executors\":[{\"kind\":\"cli-opencode\",\"model\":\"opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"max\",\"label\":\"deepseek\",\"iterations\":5,\"timeoutSeconds\":2400}]}\n---\nResearch how to make an agent ask the operator for a decision through its runtime's native ask-question tool instead of ending a turn with a prose A/B/C option menu. The runtimes in scope are Claude Code (AskUserQuestion), Codex (request_user_input), Pi (the @juicesharp/rpiv-ask-user-question extension), OpenCode (its built-in question tool) and every other cli runtime in this repo that has one: Devin, Cursor, DSH (DeepSeek Harness) and Hermes. Prove for each runtime whether a tool exists and give its exact name. Read-only: write only under the research artifact directory. Cite file:line, or a binary or doc source, for every finding.\n\nKnown failure evidence, which the research must verify, not assume:\n(1) .skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md §4 says \"Ask as a structured choice\", and its §5 fallback, \"a numbered list of named options with the recommendation marked\", literally allows a prose menu.\n(2) AGENTS.md Gate 3 teaches a prose \"A) Existing B) New C) Related D) Skip\" format, and that file is always loaded.\n(3) Nothing enforces the rule. The Claude Stop hooks in .claude/settings.json are all async.\n\nQuestions:\nQ1. Per runtime: does an ask tool exist, what is its exact name, and is it always available or gated by a mode or flag?\nQ2. Per runtime: which hook or plugin event can deterministically detect a turn that ends in a prose option menu with no ask-tool call, and block or re-prompt it? Candidates: Claude Stop with decision:block, Codex Stop, Pi and OpenCode plugin events, Devin Stop, Cursor afterAgentResponse, DSH and Hermes equivalents. Say which events can only observe and cannot block.\nQ3. What detector heuristic works (lettered or numbered option list plus a question near the end of the last assistant message, with no ask-tool call in the turn), and what is its false-positive risk on ordinary numbered steps, summaries and code blocks? Give a test-fixture set.\nQ4. How should this be wired through .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/hook-registry.json, sync-hook-registrations.cjs and the .skilled/hooks/<name>/<runtime>/ layout? Reuse the per-runtime adapters and transcript readers in .skilled/hooks/decision-capture/. Also: the loop guard (stop_hook_active), sync versus async, and the escape hatch.\nQ5. What exact rule-text amendments should go into communication-handoff.md §4/§5 and AGENTS.md Gate 3, kept inside the REPO RULES.md \"ask-surface carve-out\"? Should the prose fallback stay for runtimes without a tool?\nEnd with a ranked, phase-able implementation plan.\n---\ndeepseek\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"concurrency\":1,\"executors\":[{\"kind\":\"cli-opencode\",\"model\":\"opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"max\",\"label\":\"deepseek\",\"iterations\":5,\"timeoutSeconds\":2400}]}\n---\nResearch how to make an agent ask the operator for a decision through its runtime's native ask-question tool instead of ending a turn with a prose A/B/C option menu. The runtimes in scope are Claude Code (AskUserQuestion), Codex (request_user_input), Pi (the @juicesharp/rpiv-ask-user-question extension), OpenCode (its built-in question tool) and every other cli runtime in this repo that has one: Devin, Cursor, DSH (DeepSeek Harness) and Hermes. Prove for each runtime whether a tool exists and give its exact name. Read-only: write only under the research artifact directory. Cite file:line, or a binary or doc source, for every finding.\n\nKnown failure evidence, which the research must verify, not assume:\n(1) .skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md §4 says \"Ask as a structured choice\", and its §5 fallback, \"a numbered list of named options with the recommendation marked\", literally allows a prose menu.\n(2) AGENTS.md Gate 3 teaches a prose \"A) Existing B) New C) Related D) Skip\" format, and that file is always loaded.\n(3) Nothing enforces the rule. The Claude Stop hooks in .claude/settings.json are all async.\n\nQuestions:\nQ1. Per runtime: does an ask tool exist, what is its exact name, and is it always available or gated by a mode or flag?\nQ2. Per runtime: which hook or plugin event can deterministically detect a turn that ends in a prose option menu with no ask-tool call, and block or re-prompt it? Candidates: Claude Stop with decision:block, Codex Stop, Pi and OpenCode plugin events, Devin Stop, Cursor afterAgentResponse, DSH and Hermes equivalents. Say which events can only observe and cannot block.\nQ3. What detector heuristic works (lettered or numbered option list plus a question near the end of the last assistant message, with no ask-tool call in the turn), and what is its false-positive risk on ordinary numbered steps, summaries and code blocks? Give a test-fixture set.\nQ4. How should this be wired through .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/hook-registry.json, sync-hook-registrations.cjs and the .skilled/hooks/<name>/<runtime>/ layout? Reuse the per-runtime adapters and transcript readers in .skilled/hooks/decision-capture/. Also: the loop guard (stop_hook_active), sync versus async, and the escape hatch.\nQ5. What exact rule-text amendments should go into communication-handoff.md §4/§5 and AGENTS.md Gate 3, kept inside the REPO RULES.md \"ask-surface carve-out\"? Should the prose fallback stay for runtimes without a tool?\nEnd with a ranked, phase-able implementation plan.\n---\ndeepseek\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cat specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/fanout.json; echo \\\"---\\\"; cat specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/topic.txt | head -30; echo \\\"---\\\"; ls specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133078511,"end":1794133079088}}}}
