{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133175238,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1baab8366002xJkzZ38f1eeLfK","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baab7c06001nhWkmfeg92HjSl","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5b44388797d1c2b","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - Ask-Surface Enforcement\ndescription: Strategy packet for the deepseek fan-out lineage researching native ask-question surfaces and turn-end enforcement.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Ask-Surface Enforcement\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the `deepseek` lineage. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next across five iterations.\n\n### Mutability\n\nAnalyst-owned sections stay stable; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nMake an agent ask the operator for a decision through its runtime's native ask-question tool instead of ending a turn with a prose A/B/C option menu: prove the tool and the enforceable turn-end event for Claude Code, Codex, Pi, OpenCode, Devin, Cursor, DSH and Hermes, define a low-false-positive detector, wire it through the hook registry, and amend the rule text.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Per runtime: does an ask tool exist, what is its exact name, and is it always available or gated by a mode or flag?\n- [ ] Per runtime: which hook or plugin event can deterministically detect a turn that ends in a prose option menu with no ask-tool call, and block or re-prompt it? Which events can only observe?\n- [ ] What detector heuristic works (lettered or numbered option list plus a question near the end of the last assistant message, with no ask-tool call in the turn), and what is its false-positive risk on ordinary numbered steps, summaries and code blocks?\n- [ ] How should this be wired through hook-registry.json, sync-hook-registrations.cjs and the .skilled/hooks/<name>/<runtime>/ layout, reusing the decision-capture adapters, with the loop guard, sync versus async, and the escape hatch?\n- [ ] What exact rule-text amendments should go into communication-handoff.md §4/§5 and AGENTS.md Gate 3 inside the REPO RULES.md ask-surface carve-out, and should the prose fallback stay for runtimes without a tool?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not implementing the hook in this run; report findings, wiring design and a ranked plan only.\n- Not editing any rule file, hook registry or settings file outside the lineage directory.\n- Not re-litigating whether the operator wants enforcement; that decision is already made.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Five iterations completed (`max-iterations` stop policy).\n- No new evidence available for a question after two consecutive iterations on the same focus.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Approaches investigated and eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n\nIteration 1: Claude Code. Prove `AskUserQuestion` exists, prove the Stop hook payload carries `last_assistant_message`, and prove every Claude Stop hook in `.claude/settings.json` is async.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: `.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md` §4-§5, `AGENTS.md` §2 Gate 3, `REPO RULES.md` §4 ask-surface carve-out, `.claude/settings.json` hooks, `.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/hook-registry.json`, `sync-hook-registrations.cjs`.\n- Reuse candidates: `completion-evidence-stop` Stop sentinel (Claude/Codex/Devin) and its Cursor `afterAgentResponse` sibling; the `decision-capture` per-runtime adapters and transcript readers; `chat-questions.mjs` option-line detector.\n- Integration points: hook registry entry, generated `.claude/settings.json` / `.codex/hooks.json` / `.cursor/hooks.json` / `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, Pi extension symlink, OpenCode plugin.\n- Constraints: read-only outside the lineage; Hermes may no longer exist in this repo.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-08T10:19:14Z\n","path":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - Ask-Surface Enforcement\\ndescription: Strategy packet for the deepseek fan-out lineage researching native ask-question surfaces and turn-end enforcement.\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - Ask-Surface Enforcement\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the `deepseek` lineage. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next across five iterations.\\n\\n### Mutability\\n\\nAnalyst-owned sections stay stable; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nMake an agent ask the operator for a decision through its runtime's native ask-question tool instead of ending a turn with a prose A/B/C option menu: prove the tool and the enforceable turn-end event for Claude Code, Codex, Pi, OpenCode, Devin, Cursor, DSH and Hermes, define a low-false-positive detector, wire it through the hook registry, and amend the rule text.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [ ] Per runtime: does an ask tool exist, what is its exact name, and is it always available or gated by a mode or flag?\\n- [ ] Per runtime: which hook or plugin event can deterministically detect a turn that ends in a prose option menu with no ask-tool call, and block or re-prompt it? Which events can only observe?\\n- [ ] What detector heuristic works (lettered or numbered option list plus a question near the end of the last assistant message, with no ask-tool call in the turn), and what is its false-positive risk on ordinary numbered steps, summaries and code blocks?\\n- [ ] How should this be wired through hook-registry.json, sync-hook-registrations.cjs and the .skilled/hooks/<name>/<runtime>/ layout, reusing the decision-capture adapters, with the loop guard, sync versus async, and the escape hatch?\\n- [ ] What exact rule-text amendments should go into communication-handoff.md §4/§5 and AGENTS.md Gate 3 inside the REPO RULES.md ask-surface carve-out, and should the prose fallback stay for runtimes without a tool?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Not implementing the hook in this run; report findings, wiring design and a ranked plan only.\\n- Not editing any rule file, hook registry or settings file outside the lineage directory.\\n- Not re-litigating whether the operator wants enforcement; that decision is already made.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Five iterations completed (`max-iterations` stop policy).\\n- No new evidence available for a question after two consecutive iterations on the same focus.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[Approaches investigated and eliminated]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n\\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n\\nIteration 1: Claude Code. Prove `AskUserQuestion` exists, prove the Stop hook payload carries `last_assistant_message`, and prove every Claude Stop hook in `.claude/settings.json` is async.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: `.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md` §4-§5, `AGENTS.md` §2 Gate 3, `REPO RULES.md` §4 ask-surface carve-out, `.claude/settings.json` hooks, `.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/hook-registry.json`, `sync-hook-registrations.cjs`.\\n- Reuse candidates: `completion-evidence-stop` Stop sentinel (Claude/Codex/Devin) and its Cursor `afterAgentResponse` sibling; the `decision-capture` per-runtime adapters and transcript readers; `chat-questions.mjs` option-line detector.\\n- Integration points: hook registry entry, generated `.claude/settings.json` / `.codex/hooks.json` / `.cursor/hooks.json` / `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, Pi extension symlink, OpenCode plugin.\\n- Constraints: read-only outside the lineage; Hermes may no longer exist in this repo.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 5\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-08T10:19:14Z\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133164902,"end":1794133175238}}}}
