{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133203174,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1baac167a002NYMokihe29Hrqy","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baac0e78001Uby1NJBEUD12zx","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a09bca4d00ec07f6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls .pi/extensions 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \"=== PI EVENTS ===\"; grep -rn \"pi\\.on(\" .skilled/hooks --include=\"*.ts\" | head -20; echo \"=== PI PLUGINS DOC ===\"; sed -n '1,60p' .pi/PLUGINS.md 2>/dev/null"},"output":"classifier-injection-screen.ts\ncompletion-evidence.ts\ndecision-capture.ts\ndispatch-audit.ts\ndispatch-preflight-lint.ts\ngit-message-gate.ts\ngit-preflight-advisory.ts\ngoal-context.ts\nlib\nmcp-route-guard.ts\noverlay-guard.ts\npi-cache-optimizer\npi-fast-mode-w-subagent-support\npost-edit-quality.ts\nprompt-advisor.ts\nREADME.md\nsession-compact-context.ts\nsession-relaunch.ts\nsession-start-advisories.ts\nsession-start-context.ts\n=== PI EVENTS ===\n.skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/pi/post-edit-quality.ts:21:  pi.on('tool_result', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/classifier-injection-screen/pi/classifier-injection-screen.ts:31:  pi.on('tool_result', async (event) => {\n.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/pi/overlay-guard.ts:12:  pi.on(\"tool_call\", async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-audit.ts:25:  pi.on('tool_result', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.ts:492:  pi.on('input', (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.ts:503:  pi.on('tool_call', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts:72:  api.on('input', ((event: any, ctx: FakeContext) => {\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:485:  pi.on('message_end', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:526:  pi.on('before_agent_start', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:545:  pi.on('agent_end', async (_event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/pi/decision-capture.ts:48:    pi.on('tool_result', (event, context) => {\n.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/pi/decision-capture.ts:100:    pi.on('turn_end', (_event, context) => {\n.skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/pi/mcp-route-guard.ts:12:  pi.on(\"tool_call\", async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/goal/pi/goal-context.ts:233:  pi.on('input', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/goal/pi/goal-context.ts:262:  pi.on('session_start', async (_event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/goal/pi/goal-context.ts:285:  pi.on('turn_end', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/pi/task-dispatch-guard.ts:41:  pi.on('tool_call', async (event, ctx) => {\n=== PI PLUGINS DOC ===\n# Pi Plugins\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nReference list of all pi plugins enabled for this environment, matching the\n`.pi/settings.json` `packages` array. Six npm packages install at both user\nlevel (`~/.pi/agent/npm`) and project level (`.pi/npm`); two git-source\nextensions (`pi-btw`, `pi-plan-build`) install the same way under `git/`;\n`pi-cache-optimizer` and `pi-fast-mode-w-subagent-support` load from local\nextension directories (`.pi/extensions/`). The npm manifests at both scopes\nare install artifacts and can retain packages that are no longer enabled.\nEntries are sorted alphabetically by package name.\n\n---\n\n#### @juicesharp/rpiv-ask-user-question (v2.15.0)\n[github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono/tree/main/packages/rpiv-ask-user-question](https://github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono/tree/main/packages/rpiv-ask-user-question)\n\nA structured questionnaire the model can put to you when it would otherwise guess — typed options instead of free-form replies\n\n---\n\n#### @juicesharp/rpiv-todo (v2.15.0)\n[github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono/tree/main/packages/rpiv-todo](https://github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono/tree/main/packages/rpiv-todo)\n\nA todo list for the model, rendered as a live overlay that survives /reload and conversation compaction\n\n---\n\n#### pi-blackhole (v0.5.16)\n[github.com/k0valik/pi-blackhole](https://github.com/k0valik/pi-blackhole)\n\nUnified compaction + observational memory — compresses conversation context while preserving durable observations and reflections\n\n---\n\n#### pi-btw (v0.8.0)\n[github.com/dbachelder/pi-btw](https://github.com/dbachelder/pi-btw)\n\nA pi extension for parallel side conversations with /btw\n\n---\n\n#### pi-cache-optimizer (v2.8.0)\n[github.com/jiangge/pi-cache-optimizer](https://github.com/jiangge/pi-cache-optimizer)\n\nImprove Pi prompt/KV cache hit rates — stable prompt ordering, OpenAI-compatible cache keys, proxy-compat warnings, and footer cache stats\n\n**Cache-compat overlay (`.pi/models.json`).** This repo ships a small `models.json`\nthat Pi layers on top of its login-provisioned model catalog\n(`~/.pi/agent/models-store.json`, auto-refreshed from the gateway and not a durable\nedit target). It currently sets `sendSessionAffinityHeaders: true` on the\n`opencode-go` channel (the OpenCode Zen gateway that serves DeepSeek V4 Pro / Flash\nover an OpenAI-compatible API), so a Pi session stays pinned to one upstream backend\nand the provider-side prefix cache stays warm. This also silences the extension's\nper-channel \"DeepSeek-like … missing compat\" startup warning for that channel.\n\n`supportsLongCacheRetention` is deliberately **left off**: DeepSeek's prefix cache is\nautomatic and does not need it, and the Zen gateway's support for OpenAI long\n`prompt_cache_retention` is unverified — enabling it blindly risks\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"classifier-injection-screen.ts\ncompletion-evidence.ts\ndecision-capture.ts\ndispatch-audit.ts\ndispatch-preflight-lint.ts\ngit-message-gate.ts\ngit-preflight-advisory.ts\ngoal-context.ts\nlib\nmcp-route-guard.ts\noverlay-guard.ts\npi-cache-optimizer\npi-fast-mode-w-subagent-support\npost-edit-quality.ts\nprompt-advisor.ts\nREADME.md\nsession-compact-context.ts\nsession-relaunch.ts\nsession-start-advisories.ts\nsession-start-context.ts\n=== PI EVENTS ===\n.skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/pi/post-edit-quality.ts:21:  pi.on('tool_result', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/classifier-injection-screen/pi/classifier-injection-screen.ts:31:  pi.on('tool_result', async (event) => {\n.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/pi/overlay-guard.ts:12:  pi.on(\"tool_call\", async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-audit.ts:25:  pi.on('tool_result', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.ts:492:  pi.on('input', (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.ts:503:  pi.on('tool_call', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts:72:  api.on('input', ((event: any, ctx: FakeContext) => {\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:485:  pi.on('message_end', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:526:  pi.on('before_agent_start', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:545:  pi.on('agent_end', async (_event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/pi/decision-capture.ts:48:    pi.on('tool_result', (event, context) => {\n.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/pi/decision-capture.ts:100:    pi.on('turn_end', (_event, context) => {\n.skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/pi/mcp-route-guard.ts:12:  pi.on(\"tool_call\", async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/goal/pi/goal-context.ts:233:  pi.on('input', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/goal/pi/goal-context.ts:262:  pi.on('session_start', async (_event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/goal/pi/goal-context.ts:285:  pi.on('turn_end', async (event, ctx) => {\n.skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/pi/task-dispatch-guard.ts:41:  pi.on('tool_call', async (event, ctx) => {\n=== PI PLUGINS DOC ===\n# Pi Plugins\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nReference list of all pi plugins enabled for this environment, matching the\n`.pi/settings.json` `packages` array. Six npm packages install at both user\nlevel (`~/.pi/agent/npm`) and project level (`.pi/npm`); two git-source\nextensions (`pi-btw`, `pi-plan-build`) install the same way under `git/`;\n`pi-cache-optimizer` and `pi-fast-mode-w-subagent-support` load from local\nextension directories (`.pi/extensions/`). The npm manifests at both scopes\nare install artifacts and can retain packages that are no longer enabled.\nEntries are sorted alphabetically by package name.\n\n---\n\n#### @juicesharp/rpiv-ask-user-question (v2.15.0)\n[github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono/tree/main/packages/rpiv-ask-user-question](https://github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono/tree/main/packages/rpiv-ask-user-question)\n\nA structured questionnaire the model can put to you when it would otherwise guess — typed options instead of free-form replies\n\n---\n\n#### @juicesharp/rpiv-todo (v2.15.0)\n[github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono/tree/main/packages/rpiv-todo](https://github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono/tree/main/packages/rpiv-todo)\n\nA todo list for the model, rendered as a live overlay that survives /reload and conversation compaction\n\n---\n\n#### pi-blackhole (v0.5.16)\n[github.com/k0valik/pi-blackhole](https://github.com/k0valik/pi-blackhole)\n\nUnified compaction + observational memory — compresses conversation context while preserving durable observations and reflections\n\n---\n\n#### pi-btw (v0.8.0)\n[github.com/dbachelder/pi-btw](https://github.com/dbachelder/pi-btw)\n\nA pi extension for parallel side conversations with /btw\n\n---\n\n#### pi-cache-optimizer (v2.8.0)\n[github.com/jiangge/pi-cache-optimizer](https://github.com/jiangge/pi-cache-optimizer)\n\nImprove Pi prompt/KV cache hit rates — stable prompt ordering, OpenAI-compatible cache keys, proxy-compat warnings, and footer cache stats\n\n**Cache-compat overlay (`.pi/models.json`).** This repo ships a small `models.json`\nthat Pi layers on top of its login-provisioned model catalog\n(`~/.pi/agent/models-store.json`, auto-refreshed from the gateway and not a durable\nedit target). It currently sets `sendSessionAffinityHeaders: true` on the\n`opencode-go` channel (the OpenCode Zen gateway that serves DeepSeek V4 Pro / Flash\nover an OpenAI-compatible API), so a Pi session stays pinned to one upstream backend\nand the provider-side prefix cache stays warm. This also silences the extension's\nper-channel \"DeepSeek-like … missing compat\" startup warning for that channel.\n\n`supportsLongCacheRetention` is deliberately **left off**: DeepSeek's prefix cache is\nautomatic and does not need it, and the Zen gateway's support for OpenAI long\n`prompt_cache_retention` is unverified — enabling it blindly risks\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"ls .pi/extensions 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \\\"=== PI EVENTS ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"pi\\\\.on(\\\" .skilled/hooks --include=\\\"*.ts\\\" | head -20; echo \\\"=== PI PLUGINS DOC ===\\\"; sed -n '1,60p' .pi/PLUGINS.md 2>/dev/null\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133202554,"end":1794133203174}}}}
