{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794133249683,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"id":"prt_1baacce93001jdJxfOBmnZLt6S","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baacc813001qB5JCW08glzpSV","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a2eb8209863b90365447d3447454a66aed9df5ac"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133249952,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1baacce94001QvA0DBh8aQbpzz","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baacc813001qB5JCW08glzpSV","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad9ebe6cb976c8a2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"F=/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_1baacb637001xYYr5q2Zw3cukP; sed -n '2855,2895p' $F; echo \"=== ASYNC ===\"; grep -n \"Run hooks in the background\" $F | head -3"},"output":"      \"prompt\": \"check the build\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n#### Stop decision control\n\n`Stop` and `SubagentStop` hooks can control whether Claude continues. In addition to the [JSON output fields](#json-output) available to all hooks, your hook script can return these event-specific fields:\n\n| Field | Description |\n| :- | :- |\n| `decision` | `\"block\"` prevents Claude from stopping. Omit to allow Claude to stop |\n| `reason` | Required when `decision` is `\"block\"`. Tells Claude why it should continue |\n| `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` | Non-error feedback for Claude. The conversation continues so Claude can act on it, but unlike `decision: \"block\"` it is shown in the transcript as hook feedback rather than a hook error |\n\nA hook that blocks by exiting 2 routes the same way as `reason`: Claude receives the stderr message as the explanation for why it should continue.\n\n```json theme={null}\n{\n  \"decision\": \"block\",\n  \"reason\": \"Must be provided when Claude is blocked from stopping\"\n}\n```\n\nUse `additionalContext` when the hook is working as designed and giving Claude guidance, such as \"run the test suite before finishing\". It keeps the conversation going through the same loop protections as `decision: \"block\"`, namely the `stop_hook_active` input and the 8-consecutive-continuation cap, but the transcript labels it `Stop hook feedback` and no hook error notification is shown:\n\n```json theme={null}\n{\n  \"hookSpecificOutput\": {\n    \"hookEventName\": \"Stop\",\n    \"additionalContext\": \"Please run the test suite before finishing\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### StopFailure\n\nRuns instead of [Stop](#stop) when the turn ends due to an API error. Claude Code ignores the hook's output and exit code, apart from [`terminalSequence`](#emit-terminal-notifications). Use this to log failures, send alerts, or take recovery actions when Claude can't complete a response due to rate limits, authentication problems, or other API errors.\n\n#### StopFailure input\n=== ASYNC ===\n453:| `async` | no | If `true`, runs in the background without blocking. See [Run hooks in the background](#run-hooks-in-the-background) |\n4112:## Run hooks in the background\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      \"prompt\": \"check the build\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n#### Stop decision control\n\n`Stop` and `SubagentStop` hooks can control whether Claude continues. In addition to the [JSON output fields](#json-output) available to all hooks, your hook script can return these event-specific fields:\n\n| Field | Description |\n| :- | :- |\n| `decision` | `\"block\"` prevents Claude from stopping. Omit to allow Claude to stop |\n| `reason` | Required when `decision` is `\"block\"`. Tells Claude why it should continue |\n| `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` | Non-error feedback for Claude. The conversation continues so Claude can act on it, but unlike `decision: \"block\"` it is shown in the transcript as hook feedback rather than a hook error |\n\nA hook that blocks by exiting 2 routes the same way as `reason`: Claude receives the stderr message as the explanation for why it should continue.\n\n```json theme={null}\n{\n  \"decision\": \"block\",\n  \"reason\": \"Must be provided when Claude is blocked from stopping\"\n}\n```\n\nUse `additionalContext` when the hook is working as designed and giving Claude guidance, such as \"run the test suite before finishing\". It keeps the conversation going through the same loop protections as `decision: \"block\"`, namely the `stop_hook_active` input and the 8-consecutive-continuation cap, but the transcript labels it `Stop hook feedback` and no hook error notification is shown:\n\n```json theme={null}\n{\n  \"hookSpecificOutput\": {\n    \"hookEventName\": \"Stop\",\n    \"additionalContext\": \"Please run the test suite before finishing\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### StopFailure\n\nRuns instead of [Stop](#stop) when the turn ends due to an API error. Claude Code ignores the hook's output and exit code, apart from [`terminalSequence`](#emit-terminal-notifications). Use this to log failures, send alerts, or take recovery actions when Claude can't complete a response due to rate limits, authentication problems, or other API errors.\n\n#### StopFailure input\n=== ASYNC ===\n453:| `async` | no | If `true`, runs in the background without blocking. See [Run hooks in the background](#run-hooks-in-the-background) |\n4112:## Run hooks in the background\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"F=/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_1baacb637001xYYr5q2Zw3cukP; sed -n '2855,2895p' $F; echo \\\"=== ASYNC ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"Run hooks in the background\\\" $F | head -3\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133249684,"end":1794133249952}}}}
