{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133357397,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1baade93f0029xiTLhKdEskFbY","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baade111001MtDPt010QiWULG","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8339c8a966dfe3f4","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"Stop.*block\\|block.*Stop\\|decision.*block\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references 2>/dev/null | head -15; echo \"=== CODEX HOOK DOCS ===\"; grep -rln \"codex hooks\\|Codex hooks\\|hooks.json\" .skilled/skills .skilled/docs 2>/dev/null | head -10"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:197:> **Completion-blocking note:** the rule runs only when `SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS` is enabled, and the decision to run it is made once, at the rule's own entry point, so every caller gets the same answer. A stale result reports a `warn`, which does not block: the orchestrator passes whenever no rule reports an error. `SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE` escalates that `warn` to an `error`, and only then does `--strict` exit 2. The ENFORCE flag is the warn-versus-block switch.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:741:If blocked: Stop, document blocker, request help\n=== CODEX HOOK DOCS ===\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/benchmark/reports/2026-08-11--manual-testing-playbook--ux-hooks-3/skill-benchmark-report.md\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/benchmark/reports/2026-08-11--manual-testing-playbook--ux-hooks-3/findings-and-recommendations.md\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/benchmark/reports/2026-08-11--manual-testing-playbook--ux-hooks-3/failed-runs.md\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/benchmark/reports/2026-08-11--manual-testing-playbook--ux-hooks-3/results.csv\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/benchmark/reports/2026-08-11--manual-testing-playbook--ux-hooks-3/skill-benchmark-report.jso