{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133410597,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1baaf4236001B9bQISirQCE7Kf","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1baaf3dd80018pCrlwvL5eO0i7","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-98dcd61674e02505","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":120,"offset":100,"path":".skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/references/hook-contract.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/references/hook-contract.md, lines 100-219\n100: Codex loads the full repo hook set (lifecycle and guards) from `.codex/hooks.json`.\n101: The user-global `~/.codex/hooks.json` must hold no copy of it, or every hook runs\n102: twice. `.skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs` removes such copies, backs up first,\n103: and keeps Superset and other third-party entries.\n104: \n105: ### 3.1 Tool-Level Guard Adapters (Claude / OpenCode parity)\n106: \n107: Beyond the session-lifecycle hooks, Codex mirrors the repo's guard hooks as thin\n108: adapters over the same runtime-neutral cores the Claude hooks and OpenCode plugins\n109: use. Each fails open (exit 0 on empty/malformed stdin); the two deny-capable guards\n110: emit `hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision: \"deny\"`, which Codex honors.\n111: \n112: | Event · matcher | Guard | Adapter |\n113: |---|---|---|\n114: | PreToolUse · `exec\\|Bash\\|apply_patch\\|edit` | spec-gate enforce (deny-capable) | `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/spec-gate-enforce.mjs` |\n115: | UserPromptSubmit | spec-gate classify (state only, no emit) | `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/spec-gate-classify.mjs` |\n116: | PreToolUse · `exec\\|Bash` | dispatch preflight lint (deny-capable) | `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs` |\n117: | PostToolUse · `apply_patch\\|edit` | post-edit quality | `.skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/codex/post-edit-quality.cjs` |\n118: | PostToolUse · `exec\\|Bash` | dispatch audit (observe) | `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs` |\n119: | Stop | completion-evidence sentinel (advisory) | `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/completion-evidence-stop.cjs` |\n120: | PreToolUse · `mcp__.*` | mcp route guard (dormant until an external MCP family registers) | `.skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/codex/mcp-route-guard.cjs` |\n121: \n122: > Codex delivers an `apply_patch` target path inside `tool_input.command` (the\n123: > `*** Add/Update/Delete File:` header), not a `file_path` field — filePath-driven\n124: > adapters parse the path from the patch body. A Stop hook's stdout is parsed as a\n125: > response envelope, so neutral shell scripts wired to Stop must not emit stdout.\n126: \n127: > Codex 0.160 renamed its shell tool from `exec` to `Bash`, and a matcher of\n128: > `exec` alone no longer fires for a shell call. Every shell matcher names both.\n129: > The same release hands PostToolUse the shell output as one string where older\n130: > builds handed `{stdout, stderr}`, so the audit adapter reads either shape.\n131: \n132: > Codex has no task-dispatch guard. Its `spawn_agent` call reaches PreToolUse as\n133: > `collaborationspawn_agent`, but the hook payload carries the spawn `message`\n134: > encrypted (`gAAAAA...`) beside `task_name` and `fork_turns`, so the guard has no\n135: > prompt or target to check.\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: ## 4. EVENT INPUTS\n140: \n141: Hook commands receive JSON on stdin. Current generated schemas use snake_case\n142: field names and reject unknown properties.\n143: \n144: `SessionStart` required shape:\n145: \n146: ```json\n147: {\n148:   \"session_id\": \"uuid\",\n149:   \"transcript_path\": null,\n150:   \"cwd\": \"/workspace\",\n151:   \"hook_event_name\": \"SessionStart\",\n152:   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n153:   \"permission_mode\": \"default\",\n154:   \"source\": \"startup\"\n155: }\n156: ```\n157: \n158: `source` is `startup`, `resume`, or `clear`.\n159: \n160: `UserPromptSubmit` adds turn-scoped prompt fields:\n161: \n162: ```json\n163: {\n164:   \"session_id\": \"uuid\",\n165:   \"turn_id\": \"uuid\",\n166:   \"transcript_path\": null,\n167:   \"cwd\": \"/workspace\",\n168:   \"hook_event_name\": \"UserPromptSubmit\",\n169:   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n170:   \"permission_mode\": \"default\",\n171:   \"prompt\": \"user prompt\"\n172: }\n173: ```\n174: \n175: ---\n176: \n177: ## 5. EVENT OUTPUTS\n178: \n179: Use JSON output for model-visible context:\n180: \n181: ```json\n182: {\n183:   \"hookSpecificOutput\": {\n184:     \"hookEventName\": \"UserPromptSubmit\",\n185:     \"additionalContext\": \"Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.\"\n186:   }\n187: }\n188: ```\n189: \n190: For `SessionStart`, set `\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\"` and put startup\n191: context in `additionalContext`.\n192: \n193: - Codex also accepts plain stdout for context on injecting events, but JSON is the preferred Spec Kit path because it is explicit and testable.\n194: - Context is recorded as a developer-role message in the conversation state.\n195: - Placement follows the event: `SessionStart` puts it before the first user prompt; `UserPromptSubmit` puts it after the submitted user message.\n196: \n197: ---\n198: \n199: ## 6. EXIT AND TIMEOUT SEMANTICS\n200: \n201: | Condition | Behavior |\n202: | --- | --- |\n203: | Exit `0` | Success. Output is parsed and injected when `additionalContext` is present. |\n204: | `UserPromptSubmit` exit `2` with stderr | Blocks the turn; stderr becomes the reason. |\n205: | Other non-zero exits | Fail-open. Codex logs the hook failure and continues the turn. |\n206: | Timeout | Fail-open. Default is 600 seconds unless `timeout` / `timeoutSec` is set. |\n207: \n208: Spec Kit hooks use short per-hook timeouts in registration and return `{}` on\n209: fail-open paths. The prompt hook emits a bounded stale advisory on cold-start\n210: timeout so the user can see the advisor surface is installed.\n211: \n212: ---\n213: \n214: ## 7. SPEC KIT HOOK WIRING\n215: \n216: Installed paths:\n217: \n218: - `SessionStart`: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/session-start.js`\n219: - `UserPromptSubmit`: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js`\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 220]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/references/hook-contract.md, lines 100-219\n100: Codex loads the full repo hook set (lifecycle and guards) from `.codex/hooks.json`.\n101: The user-global `~/.codex/hooks.json` must hold no copy of it, or every hook runs\n102: twice. `.skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs` removes such copies, backs up first,\n103: and keeps Superset and other third-party entries.\n104: \n105: ### 3.1 Tool-Level Guard Adapters (Claude / OpenCode parity)\n106: \n107: Beyond the session-lifecycle hooks, Codex mirrors the repo's guard hooks as thin\n108: adapters over the same runtime-neutral cores the Claude hooks and OpenCode plugins\n109: use. Each fails open (exit 0 on empty/malformed stdin); the two deny-capable guards\n110: emit `hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision: \"deny\"`, which Codex honors.\n111: \n112: | Event · matcher | Guard | Adapter |\n113: |---|---|---|\n114: | PreToolUse · `exec\\|Bash\\|apply_patch\\|edit` | spec-gate enforce (deny-capable) | `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/spec-gate-enforce.mjs` |\n115: | UserPromptSubmit | spec-gate classify (state only, no emit) | `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/spec-gate-classify.mjs` |\n116: | PreToolUse · `exec\\|Bash` | dispatch preflight lint (deny-capable) | `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs` |\n117: | PostToolUse · `apply_patch\\|edit` | post-edit quality | `.skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/codex/post-edit-quality.cjs` |\n118: | PostToolUse · `exec\\|Bash` | dispatch audit (observe) | `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs` |\n119: | Stop | completion-evidence sentinel (advisory) | `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/completion-evidence-stop.cjs` |\n120: | PreToolUse · `mcp__.*` | mcp route guard (dormant until an external MCP family registers) | `.skilled/hooks/mcp-route-guard/codex/mcp-route-guard.cjs` |\n121: \n122: > Codex delivers an `apply_patch` target path inside `tool_input.command` (the\n123: > `*** Add/Update/Delete File:` header), not a `file_path` field — filePath-driven\n124: > adapters parse the path from the patch body. A Stop hook's stdout is parsed as a\n125: > response envelope, so neutral shell scripts wired to Stop must not emit stdout.\n126: \n127: > Codex 0.160 renamed its shell tool from `exec` to `Bash`, and a matcher of\n128: > `exec` alone no longer fires for a shell call. Every shell matcher names both.\n129: > The same release hands PostToolUse the shell output as one string where older\n130: > builds handed `{stdout, stderr}`, so the audit adapter reads either shape.\n131: \n132: > Codex has no task-dispatch guard. Its `spawn_agent` call reaches PreToolUse as\n133: > `collaborationspawn_agent`, but the hook payload carries the spawn `message`\n134: > encrypted (`gAAAAA...`) beside `task_name` and `fork_turns`, so the guard has no\n135: > prompt or target to check.\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: ## 4. EVENT INPUTS\n140: \n141: Hook commands receive JSON on stdin. Current generated schemas use snake_case\n142: field names and reject unknown properties.\n143: \n144: `SessionStart` required shape:\n145: \n146: ```json\n147: {\n148:   \"session_id\": \"uuid\",\n149:   \"transcript_path\": null,\n150:   \"cwd\": \"/workspace\",\n151:   \"hook_event_name\": \"SessionStart\",\n152:   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n153:   \"permission_mode\": \"default\",\n154:   \"source\": \"startup\"\n155: }\n156: ```\n157: \n158: `source` is `startup`, `resume`, or `clear`.\n159: \n160: `UserPromptSubmit` adds turn-scoped prompt fields:\n161: \n162: ```json\n163: {\n164:   \"session_id\": \"uuid\",\n165:   \"turn_id\": \"uuid\",\n166:   \"transcript_path\": null,\n167:   \"cwd\": \"/workspace\",\n168:   \"hook_event_name\": \"UserPromptSubmit\",\n169:   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n170:   \"permission_mode\": \"default\",\n171:   \"prompt\": \"user prompt\"\n172: }\n173: ```\n174: \n175: ---\n176: \n177: ## 5. EVENT OUTPUTS\n178: \n179: Use JSON output for model-visible context:\n180: \n181: ```json\n182: {\n183:   \"hookSpecificOutput\": {\n184:     \"hookEventName\": \"UserPromptSubmit\",\n185:     \"additionalContext\": \"Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.\"\n186:   }\n187: }\n188: ```\n189: \n190: For `SessionStart`, set `\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\"` and put startup\n191: context in `additionalContext`.\n192: \n193: - Codex also accepts plain stdout for context on injecting events, but JSON is the preferred Spec Kit path because it is explicit and testable.\n194: - Context is recorded as a developer-role message in the conversation state.\n195: - Placement follows the event: `SessionStart` puts it before the first user prompt; `UserPromptSubmit` puts it after the submitted user message.\n196: \n197: ---\n198: \n199: ## 6. EXIT AND TIMEOUT SEMANTICS\n200: \n201: | Condition | Behavior |\n202: | --- | --- |\n203: | Exit `0` | Success. Output is parsed and injected when `additionalContext` is present. |\n204: | `UserPromptSubmit` exit `2` with stderr | Blocks the turn; stderr becomes the reason. |\n205: | Other non-zero exits | Fail-open. Codex logs the hook failure and continues the turn. |\n206: | Timeout | Fail-open. Default is 600 seconds unless `timeout` / `timeoutSec` is set. |\n207: \n208: Spec Kit hooks use short per-hook timeouts in registration and return `{}` on\n209: fail-open paths. The prompt hook emits a bounded stale advisory on cold-start\n210: timeout so the user can see the advisor surface is installed.\n211: \n212: ---\n213: \n214: ## 7. SPEC KIT HOOK WIRING\n215: \n216: Installed paths:\n217: \n218: - `SessionStart`: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/session-start.js`\n219: - `UserPromptSubmit`: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js`\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 220]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 120, \"offset\": 100, \"path\": \".skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/references/hook-contract.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133410358,"end":1794133410597}}}}
