{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794133483482,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"id":"prt_1bab05fda001UriLLqVNTiXc6h","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab05870001mC1vectntNjFxB","type":"step-start","snapshot":"217b6befe64bd4433545dd35d96183e3f98b568f"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133483803,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1bab05fdb001z10NVtI3VUcRbm","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab05870001mC1vectntNjFxB","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5d1c7d4ff67ab6a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"ask\\|question\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/cursor-tools.md | head -20; echo \"=== CURSOR HOOKS ===\"; grep -n \"afterAgentResponse\\|block\\|deny\\|permission\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/hook-contract.md | head -25; echo \"=== DSH HOOKS ===\"; grep -n \"event\\|block\\|tools/result\\|agent/status\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-deepseek-harness/references/guards-and-hooks.md | head -25"},"output":".skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:27:Covers all built-in capabilities available in Devin CLI, highlights what is unique compared to other CLI executors, and provides the 4-tier permission model for task routing decisions.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:31:- Choosing whether to delegate a task to Devin CLI or handle it in the calling AI\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:32:- Understanding which Devin tools and permission modes to use for different task types\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:73:- Isolating subtask context from the parent conversation\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:75:**Compared to other CLI executors:** Most CLI executors lack native subagent spawning. Devin's `run_subagent` is a first-class tool that the agent calls automatically when a task benefits from independent work.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:100:# Without a task description, continues from where you left off\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:105:- Long-running tasks (migrations, batch jobs, large refactors)\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:120:- `adaptive` mode auto-selects the best model per task\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:123:- Cost optimization: use `swe` / `swe-1-6-fast` for cheap tasks, `opus` for deep reasoning\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:138:- Tasks that benefit from a specific provider's model\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:141:- Tasks where model diversity helps cross-validation\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:212:| Clarification | Ask for input when needed | `ask_user_question` tool (not available to subagents) |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:213:| Task tracking | Internal task management | Built into session context |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:263:Deny is checked before ask, and ask before allow. A deny rule always wins. Organization-level denials cannot be overridden.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:395:- Isolating subtask context from the parent conversation\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:398:**Avoid for:** Tasks that share context with the parent or need the parent's full conversation history.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:402:- Long-running tasks that exceed local session time\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:407:**Avoid for:** Quick edits that complete faster locally; tasks involving sensitive data without confirming cloud isolation.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:414:- `gpt` / `codex` when OpenAI-model strengths fit the task\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:416:**Avoid for:** Tasks where a single model already handles well and switching adds overhead.\n=== CURSOR HOOKS ===\n83:Confirmed documented event names: `sessionStart`, `sessionEnd`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `postToolUseFailure`, `subagentStart`, `subagentStop`, `beforeShellExecution`, `afterShellExecution`, `beforeMCPExecution`, `afterMCPExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `afterFileEdit`, `beforeSubmitPrompt`, `preCompact`, `stop`, `afterAgentResponse`, `afterAgentThought` (plus Tab-completion and `workspaceOpen` app-lifecycle events that are editor-only, not agent-session events).\n95:  \"permission\": \"allow\",\n101:`permission` is `\"allow\"`, `\"deny\"`, or `\"ask\"`.\n=== DSH HOOKS ===\n35:Twenty adapters are registered by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, and `.dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml` inserts the bundle into every dsh lineage the deep-loop runner builds and into an operator's interactive session. Four of them are interactive-only: the lineage patch inserts a marker row, `repo-guards-lineage-leaf`, and those four check it at event time (section 4).\n41:The saved `workspace-write` probe denied a write under `$HOME` outside the cwd, but allowed a sibling path under the OS temp directory. A lineage can therefore write inside another lineage's disposable `DSH_HOME` when both homes are under that temp directory. Keep the observed preventive boundary qualified by this exception, and do not treat separate temp homes as an enforced boundary between lineages. Evidence: `specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/013-dsh-live-contract-pin/evidence/confinement.md`.\n47:The harness raises these events, and a plugin can attach to them (research synthesis section 9.6):\n53:| `tools/result` | Read a call's final outcome, including the live answer value |\n56:| `agent/status` | Act when the agent goes idle |\n58:| `session/event` | Read each committed session entry, such as `compaction/end` or a steered user message |\n81:- It has no `PreCompact` or `SessionEnd` event.\n89:| Adapter | DSH event | Scope | Error policy |\n106:| `session-compact-context` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Session-prime `compact` output | Log and continue |\n107:| `decision-capture` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | `ask_user_question` answers and late timed replies | Log and continue |\n108:| `goal-manage` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | `/goal-dsh`, `dsh_goal`, goal brief, verify note | Log and continue, interactive only |\n112:Five of these can refuse a call: `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `spec-gate-enforce`, `mcp-route-guard`, `git-message-gate` and `overlay-guard`. The rest inject context, attach an advisory, record a row or ask for another step. Context adapters call `agent.inject` or return `additionalContexts`, and a core error in one of them never blocks a tool call.\n120:The guards patch sets `promptAdvisor: true`. The lineage patch cannot override that row, because the runner applies it before the guards patch inserts the bundle, and a patch for a row that does not exist yet is dropped with a `patch: entry \"repo-guards\" not found` warning. So the lineage patch inserts its own marker plugin, and the bundle reads the marker when an event fires, since plugin `apply` order is not awaited across rows.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:27:Covers all built-in capabilities available in Devin CLI, highlights what is unique compared to other CLI executors, and provides the 4-tier permission model for task routing decisions.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:31:- Choosing whether to delegate a task to Devin CLI or handle it in the calling AI\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:32:- Understanding which Devin tools and permission modes to use for different task types\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:73:- Isolating subtask context from the parent conversation\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:75:**Compared to other CLI executors:** Most CLI executors lack native subagent spawning. Devin's `run_subagent` is a first-class tool that the agent calls automatically when a task benefits from independent work.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:100:# Without a task description, continues from where you left off\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:105:- Long-running tasks (migrations, batch jobs, large refactors)\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:120:- `adaptive` mode auto-selects the best model per task\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:123:- Cost optimization: use `swe` / `swe-1-6-fast` for cheap tasks, `opus` for deep reasoning\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:138:- Tasks that benefit from a specific provider's model\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:141:- Tasks where model diversity helps cross-validation\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:212:| Clarification | Ask for input when needed | `ask_user_question` tool (not available to subagents) |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:213:| Task tracking | Internal task management | Built into session context |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:263:Deny is checked before ask, and ask before allow. A deny rule always wins. Organization-level denials cannot be overridden.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:395:- Isolating subtask context from the parent conversation\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:398:**Avoid for:** Tasks that share context with the parent or need the parent's full conversation history.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:402:- Long-running tasks that exceed local session time\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:407:**Avoid for:** Quick edits that complete faster locally; tasks involving sensitive data without confirming cloud isolation.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:414:- `gpt` / `codex` when OpenAI-model strengths fit the task\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md:416:**Avoid for:** Tasks where a single model already handles well and switching adds overhead.\n=== CURSOR HOOKS ===\n83:Confirmed documented event names: `sessionStart`, `sessionEnd`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `postToolUseFailure`, `subagentStart`, `subagentStop`, `beforeShellExecution`, `afterShellExecution`, `beforeMCPExecution`, `afterMCPExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `afterFileEdit`, `beforeSubmitPrompt`, `preCompact`, `stop`, `afterAgentResponse`, `afterAgentThought` (plus Tab-completion and `workspaceOpen` app-lifecycle events that are editor-only, not agent-session events).\n95:  \"permission\": \"allow\",\n101:`permission` is `\"allow\"`, `\"deny\"`, or `\"ask\"`.\n=== DSH HOOKS ===\n35:Twenty adapters are registered by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, and `.dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml` inserts the bundle into every dsh lineage the deep-loop runner builds and into an operator's interactive session. Four of them are interactive-only: the lineage patch inserts a marker row, `repo-guards-lineage-leaf`, and those four check it at event time (section 4).\n41:The saved `workspace-write` probe denied a write under `$HOME` outside the cwd, but allowed a sibling path under the OS temp directory. A lineage can therefore write inside another lineage's disposable `DSH_HOME` when both homes are under that temp directory. Keep the observed preventive boundary qualified by this exception, and do not treat separate temp homes as an enforced boundary between lineages. Evidence: `specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/013-dsh-live-contract-pin/evidence/confinement.md`.\n47:The harness raises these events, and a plugin can attach to them (research synthesis section 9.6):\n53:| `tools/result` | Read a call's final outcome, including the live answer value |\n56:| `agent/status` | Act when the agent goes idle |\n58:| `session/event` | Read each committed session entry, such as `compaction/end` or a steered user message |\n81:- It has no `PreCompact` or `SessionEnd` event.\n89:| Adapter | DSH event | Scope | Error policy |\n106:| `session-compact-context` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Session-prime `compact` output | Log and continue |\n107:| `decision-capture` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | `ask_user_question` answers and late timed replies | Log and continue |\n108:| `goal-manage` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | `/goal-dsh`, `dsh_goal`, goal brief, verify note | Log and continue, interactive only |\n112:Five of these can refuse a call: `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `spec-gate-enforce`, `mcp-route-guard`, `git-message-gate` and `overlay-guard`. The rest inject context, attach an advisory, record a row or ask for another step. Context adapters call `agent.inject` or return `additionalContexts`, and a core error in one of them never blocks a tool call.\n120:The guards patch sets `promptAdvisor: true`. The lineage patch cannot override that row, because the runner applies it before the guards patch inserts the bundle, and a patch for a row that does not exist yet is dropped with a `patch: entry \"repo-guards\" not found` warning. So the lineage patch inserts its own marker plugin, and the bundle reads the marker when an event fires, since plugin `apply` order is not awaited across rows.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"ask\\\\|question\\\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/references/devin-tools.md .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/cursor-tools.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== CURSOR HOOKS ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"afterAgentResponse\\\\|block\\\\|deny\\\\|permission\\\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/hook-contract.md | head -25; echo \\\"=== DSH HOOKS ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"event\\\\|block\\\\|tools/result\\\\|agent/status\\\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-deepseek-harness/references/guards-and-hooks.md | head -25\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133483483,"end":1794133483803}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794133484597,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"id":"prt_1bab06435001jqmMTnU6v0pNGc","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab05870001mC1vectntNjFxB","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"217b6befe64bd4433545dd35d96183e3f98b568f","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":353,"output":217,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":211968,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794133485816,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"id":"prt_1bab068f8001n963OOG2zvpX1B","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab0643b00138V0u4lqpKZ4y1","type":"step-start","snapshot":"217b6befe64bd4433545dd35d96183e3f98b568f"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133488183,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1bab0701b0026xtM3bh6jCIiFR","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab0643b00138V0u4lqpKZ4y1","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c6dba5a1a2f41f5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '45,115p' .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-deepseek-harness/references/guards-and-hooks.md; echo \"=== CURSOR TOOLS ===\"; grep -n \"| \\`\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/cursor-tools.md | head -30"},"output":"## 2. HARNESS SEAMS\n\nThe harness raises these events, and a plugin can attach to them (research synthesis section 9.6):\n\n| Seam | What a guard can do there |\n|---|---|\n| `tools/pre-execute` | Deny or ask before a tool call |\n| `tools/post-execute` | Block with feedback or attach context after a tool call |\n| `tools/result` | Read a call's final outcome, including the live answer value |\n| `agent/pre-step` | Add messages to a model step |\n| `agent/turn-stopping` | Force another step before the turn ends |\n| `agent/status` | Act when the agent goes idle |\n| `agent/created`, `agent/disposed` | Session start and end work |\n| `session/event` | Read each committed session entry, such as `compaction/end` or a steered user message |\n| `fs/write-intent`, `fs/edit-intent`, `fs/delete-intent` | File-intent checks |\n\nTool arguments cannot be rewritten at `tools/pre-execute`, so a guard denies, it never edits. Harness tool names are lowercase (`bash`, `write`, `edit`, `subagent`), so a matcher written for capitalized tool names selects nothing. The harness's own guard package is loop hygiene, not repository policy.\n\n---\n\n## 3. DELIVERY: ONE REPO-LOCAL PLUGIN\n\nGuards ship as one hand-authored Cordis bundle under `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/`, inserted by `.dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml` with a relative plugin name. The bundle calls the same shared guard cores the Pi extensions bridge, and each adapter pins its error policy explicitly.\n\nThe bundle uses Pi's layout. Each file in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/` is a relative link to the real adapter in `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/`, or in the owning skill's `hooks/dsh/` folder with an index link in the hook library. Node resolves the link before it resolves the adapter's imports, so each adapter's imports are written for its real folder. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` checks the links through `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`.\n\n**Observed:** relative plugin loading works before any provider call. A stub plugin inserted by relative path wrote its marker file in the temp cwd during the keyless run that then failed on the missing key (`specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/002-dsh-offline-contract-pin/evidence/plugin-boot.txt`). The real bundle loads the same way: the keyless guards boot reached `MISSING_CREDENTIAL` with zero `did not activate` lines, so a guard loaded by this patch is active before the model is asked anything.\n\n**Not proven by that boot:** that any adapter's verdict on a live tool call is right. The bundle suite exercises the adapters against fixtures, and no keyed dispatch has run a model against them.\n\n### Why Not the Claude Hook Bridge\n\nThe experimental `dsh-hooks-claude-code` bridge would reuse the hook scripts as they are. It stays a fallback, for three reasons from the research:\n\n- It is not in the installed package, so a per-dispatch `$DSH_HOME` would need a package install per dispatch.\n- An unreadable or unparsable hook config makes it log a warning and run no hooks while the agent still starts, which is fail-open for every guard.\n- It has no `PreCompact` or `SessionEnd` event.\n\n---\n\n## 4. THE ADAPTER SET\n\nEvery adapter below is registered by `index.mjs`. `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md` section 4 owns this table, and it is repeated here because a dispatch decision needs it beside the seam list.\n\n| Adapter | DSH event | Scope | Error policy |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `dispatch-audit` | `tools/post-execute` | `bash` | Log and continue |\n| `dispatch-preflight-lint` | `tools/pre-execute` | `bash` | Log and deny on core failure |\n| `spec-gate-classify` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | Log and continue |\n| `spec-gate-enforce` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `bash` | Log and deny on core failure |\n| `completion-evidence` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn | Log and continue |\n| `task-dispatch-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `subagent`, `subagent_fork` | Log and continue |\n| `post-edit-quality` | `tools/post-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | Log and continue |\n| `mcp-route-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `mcp__*` | Log and deny on core failure, and deny a `code_mode` tool outside the four-tool allowlist |\n| `classifier-injection-screen` | `tools/post-execute` | `web_fetch`, `web_search`, `mcp__*` | Log and continue |\n| `goal-context` | `agent/created` | `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` chat slice | Log and continue |\n| `session-start-context` | `agent/created` | Session-prime output | Log and continue |\n| `prompt-advisor` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | Log and continue, interactive only |\n| `git-preflight-advisory` | `tools/post-execute` | Bash Git commands | Log and continue, add context |\n| `git-message-gate` | `tools/pre-execute` | Bash commands covered by the message contract | Log unexpected errors and continue, deny on `ContractError` |\n| `overlay-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | Log and allow, deny only a path an overlay owns |\n| `session-compact-context` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Session-prime `compact` output | Log and continue |\n| `decision-capture` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | `ask_user_question` answers and late timed replies | Log and continue |\n| `goal-manage` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | `/goal-dsh`, `dsh_goal`, goal brief, verify note | Log and continue, interactive only |\n| `session-start-advisories` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | The six warn-only session-start guards | Log each failing guard and continue, interactive only |\n| `session-stop-context` | `agent/disposed` | `session-stop.js` autosave | Log and continue, interactive only |\n\nFive of these can refuse a call: `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `spec-gate-enforce`, `mcp-route-guard`, `git-message-gate` and `overlay-guard`. The rest inject context, attach an advisory, record a row or ask for another step. Context adapters call `agent.inject` or return `additionalContexts`, and a core error in one of them never blocks a tool call.\n\n`dispatch-audit`, `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `git-preflight-advisory`, `mcp-route-guard` and `session-start-advisories` resolve the checkout from the adapter file, not the session cwd. A dsh session runs in a lineage or scratch folder, where a cwd-relative rule tree would be empty and the lint would allow every command. `git-message-gate` is a policy gate, so a contract violation or an unreadable contract returns `deny`.\n\n=== CURSOR TOOLS ===\n125:| Native worktree | `-w`/`--worktree` | Never passed | Not wired — would double-isolate against the runtime's own lineage directories |\n126:| Cloud worker | `cursor-agent worker` | Never invoked | Out of scope — different execution shape entirely |\n127:| Plugin marketplace | `cursor-agent plugin marketplace` | Never invoked | Operator-only, persistent/shared surface |\n128:| MCP client | `cursor-agent mcp ...` / `--approve-mcps` | `--approve-mcps` passed when a task explicitly needs MCP tools | Supported, gated by explicit task need |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 2. HARNESS SEAMS\n\nThe harness raises these events, and a plugin can attach to them (research synthesis section 9.6):\n\n| Seam | What a guard can do there |\n|---|---|\n| `tools/pre-execute` | Deny or ask before a tool call |\n| `tools/post-execute` | Block with feedback or attach context after a tool call |\n| `tools/result` | Read a call's final outcome, including the live answer value |\n| `agent/pre-step` | Add messages to a model step |\n| `agent/turn-stopping` | Force another step before the turn ends |\n| `agent/status` | Act when the agent goes idle |\n| `agent/created`, `agent/disposed` | Session start and end work |\n| `session/event` | Read each committed session entry, such as `compaction/end` or a steered user message |\n| `fs/write-intent`, `fs/edit-intent`, `fs/delete-intent` | File-intent checks |\n\nTool arguments cannot be rewritten at `tools/pre-execute`, so a guard denies, it never edits. Harness tool names are lowercase (`bash`, `write`, `edit`, `subagent`), so a matcher written for capitalized tool names selects nothing. The harness's own guard package is loop hygiene, not repository policy.\n\n---\n\n## 3. DELIVERY: ONE REPO-LOCAL PLUGIN\n\nGuards ship as one hand-authored Cordis bundle under `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/`, inserted by `.dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml` with a relative plugin name. The bundle calls the same shared guard cores the Pi extensions bridge, and each adapter pins its error policy explicitly.\n\nThe bundle uses Pi's layout. Each file in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/` is a relative link to the real adapter in `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/`, or in the owning skill's `hooks/dsh/` folder with an index link in the hook library. Node resolves the link before it resolves the adapter's imports, so each adapter's imports are written for its real folder. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` checks the links through `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`.\n\n**Observed:** relative plugin loading works before any provider call. A stub plugin inserted by relative path wrote its marker file in the temp cwd during the keyless run that then failed on the missing key (`specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/002-dsh-offline-contract-pin/evidence/plugin-boot.txt`). The real bundle loads the same way: the keyless guards boot reached `MISSING_CREDENTIAL` with zero `did not activate` lines, so a guard loaded by this patch is active before the model is asked anything.\n\n**Not proven by that boot:** that any adapter's verdict on a live tool call is right. The bundle suite exercises the adapters against fixtures, and no keyed dispatch has run a model against them.\n\n### Why Not the Claude Hook Bridge\n\nThe experimental `dsh-hooks-claude-code` bridge would reuse the hook scripts as they are. It stays a fallback, for three reasons from the research:\n\n- It is not in the installed package, so a per-dispatch `$DSH_HOME` would need a package install per dispatch.\n- An unreadable or unparsable hook config makes it log a warning and run no hooks while the agent still starts, which is fail-open for every guard.\n- It has no `PreCompact` or `SessionEnd` event.\n\n---\n\n## 4. THE ADAPTER SET\n\nEvery adapter below is registered by `index.mjs`. `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md` section 4 owns this table, and it is repeated here because a dispatch decision needs it beside the seam list.\n\n| Adapter | DSH event | Scope | Error policy |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `dispatch-audit` | `tools/post-execute` | `bash` | Log and continue |\n| `dispatch-preflight-lint` | `tools/pre-execute` | `bash` | Log and deny on core failure |\n| `spec-gate-classify` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | Log and continue |\n| `spec-gate-enforce` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `bash` | Log and deny on core failure |\n| `completion-evidence` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn | Log and continue |\n| `task-dispatch-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `subagent`, `subagent_fork` | Log and continue |\n| `post-edit-quality` | `tools/post-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | Log and continue |\n| `mcp-route-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `mcp__*` | Log and deny on core failure, and deny a `code_mode` tool outside the four-tool allowlist |\n| `classifier-injection-screen` | `tools/post-execute` | `web_fetch`, `web_search`, `mcp__*` | Log and continue |\n| `goal-context` | `agent/created` | `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` chat slice | Log and continue |\n| `session-start-context` | `agent/created` | Session-prime output | Log and continue |\n| `prompt-advisor` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | Log and continue, interactive only |\n| `git-preflight-advisory` | `tools/post-execute` | Bash Git commands | Log and continue, add context |\n| `git-message-gate` | `tools/pre-execute` | Bash commands covered by the message contract | Log unexpected errors and continue, deny on `ContractError` |\n| `overlay-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | Log and allow, deny only a path an overlay owns |\n| `session-compact-context` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Session-prime `compact` output | Log and continue |\n| `decision-capture` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | `ask_user_question` answers and late timed replies | Log and continue |\n| `goal-manage` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | `/goal-dsh`, `dsh_goal`, goal brief, verify note | Log and continue, interactive only |\n| `session-start-advisories` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | The six warn-only session-start guards | Log each failing guard and continue, interactive only |\n| `session-stop-context` | `agent/disposed` | `session-stop.js` autosave | Log and continue, interactive only |\n\nFive of these can refuse a call: `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `spec-gate-enforce`, `mcp-route-guard`, `git-message-gate` and `overlay-guard`. The rest inject context, attach an advisory, record a row or ask for another step. Context adapters call `agent.inject` or return `additionalContexts`, and a core error in one of them never blocks a tool call.\n\n`dispatch-audit`, `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `git-preflight-advisory`, `mcp-route-guard` and `session-start-advisories` resolve the checkout from the adapter file, not the session cwd. A dsh session runs in a lineage or scratch folder, where a cwd-relative rule tree would be empty and the lint would allow every command. `git-message-gate` is a policy gate, so a contract violation or an unreadable contract returns `deny`.\n\n=== CURSOR TOOLS ===\n125:| Native worktree | `-w`/`--worktree` | Never passed | Not wired — would double-isolate against the runtime's own lineage directories |\n126:| Cloud worker | `cursor-agent worker` | Never invoked | Out of scope — different execution shape entirely |\n127:| Plugin marketplace | `cursor-agent plugin marketplace` | Never invoked | Operator-only, persistent/shared surface |\n128:| MCP client | `cursor-agent mcp ...` / `--approve-mcps` | `--approve-mcps` passed when a task explicitly needs MCP tools | Supported, gated by explicit task need |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"sed -n '45,115p' .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-deepseek-harness/references/guards-and-hooks.md; echo \\\"=== CURSOR TOOLS ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"| \\\\`\\\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/cursor-tools.md | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133487643,"end":1794133488183}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794133488989,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"id":"prt_1bab0755d001VTlWQldzV9hCsf","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab0643b00138V0u4lqpKZ4y1","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"217b6befe64bd4433545dd35d96183e3f98b568f","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1794,"output":124,"reasoning":211,"cache":{"read":212480,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794133490070,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"id":"prt_1bab079960015GXTcfSrSM3xOl","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab075640016L0BYasg9H0IOI","type":"step-start","snapshot":"217b6befe64bd4433545dd35d96183e3f98b568f"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133491164,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1bab07b64001AJnJxXtiSS36oZ","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab075640016L0BYasg9H0IOI","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5fcef897e695edc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/cursor-tools.md"},"output":"---\ntitle: \"Cursor CLI Unique Capabilities\"\ndescription: \"Cursor CLI surfaces with no sibling analog: native git worktree isolation, the cloud worker, the plugin marketplace, and MCP client support.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"cursor worktree\"\n  - \"cursor cloud worker\"\n  - \"cursor plugin marketplace\"\n  - \"cursor mcp client\"\n  - \"cursor unique surfaces\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.4.1.0\n---\n\n# Cursor CLI Unique Capabilities\n\nReference for the Cursor CLI surfaces that have **no analog** in `cli-codex`, `cli-claude-code`, or `cli-opencode`. Each is documented as an opt-in escape hatch — this packet's default dispatch (`SKILL.md` §3) never invokes any of them automatically.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nCursor CLI ships several capabilities that go beyond \"run a prompt against a model\": native git worktree isolation, a private cloud execution worker, a plugin marketplace, and Cursor's own subagent/skill system. These surfaces are documented here as deliberate, user-invoked escape hatches.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- The operator explicitly wants an experiment tried in an isolated checkout without touching the current workspace\n- The operator explicitly wants Cursor to run agents in a remote/cloud environment rather than locally\n- The operator wants to discover or manage Cursor plugins\n- A task needs an MCP server Cursor is already configured to use\n\n### Core Principle\n\nNone of these change `cli-cursor`'s `packetKind: \"workflow\"` classification (see `030-cli-cursor-creation/003-cli-cursor-skill-packet/decision-record.md` ADR-001) — the packet's default dispatch still runs locally and writes land in this repo's checkout.\n\n---\n\n## 2. NATIVE GIT WORKTREE ISOLATION\n\n### What It Is\n\n`-w` / `--worktree [name]` starts `cursor-agent` in an isolated git worktree at `~/.cursor/worktrees/<reponame>/<name>`, rather than the current working directory. `--worktree-base <branch>` sets the base ref for the new worktree. `--skip-worktree-setup` skips any setup scripts declared in `.cursor/worktrees.json`.\n\n### Why It's Out of Scope for Orchestrated Dispatch\n\nThis repo already manages its own numbered-worktree discipline via `sk-git` (owner-scoped branches, `.worktrees/{NNNN}-{owner}-{slug}` directories). A dispatched `cursor-agent` inside a deep-loop fan-out lineage already runs inside that lineage's own isolated directory — passing `-w` on top would create a SECOND, Cursor-native worktree nested inside or alongside the first, doubling isolation in a way the runtime does not expect and has not been built to reconcile. The deep-loop executor adapter (`buildCursorLineageCommand`) never passes `-w`.\n\n### When an Operator Might Use It Directly\n\n```bash\n# Try a risky refactor in a disposable worktree, leaving the current checkout untouched\ncursor-agent -p \"Attempt an aggressive refactor of the auth module\" \\\n  -w risky-refactor --model composer-2.5 --auto-review --sandbox enabled\n\n# Base the new worktree on a specific branch\ncursor-agent -p \"Prototype the new caching layer\" \\\n  -w cache-prototype --worktree-base develop --model composer-2.5\n```\n\nThis is a direct, interactive/manual operator action — not something an orchestrated fan-out or automated pipeline in this repo should invoke on its own.\n\n---\n\n## 3. CLOUD WORKER\n\n### What It Is\n\n`cursor-agent worker` runs a private cloud worker that connects to Cursor's infrastructure to run agents in the operator's own environment remotely. It is infra-grade remote execution: Kubernetes-style health probes (`GET /healthz`, `/readyz`), a Prometheus `/metrics` endpoint, pool vs. shared assignment (`--pool`/`--pool-name`), labels, and `--auth-token-file` for operator-managed secret mounts.\n\n### Why It's Out of Scope for This Packet's Runtime Wiring\n\nThis is a fundamentally different execution shape than every other capability this packet dispatches — it stands up a long-running service, not a single bounded `-p` prompt/response round-trip. Wiring it into this repo's deep-loop runtime would mean building an entirely separate execution model (service lifecycle, health checks, secret mounts) that no sibling CLI needs and that the parent packet's spec explicitly scopes out. If a future need for genuinely remote, infra-grade Cursor execution arises, that is new scope for a dedicated future packet — not a repurposing of this one's `-p` dispatch adapter.\n\n### When an Operator Might Use It Directly\n\n```bash\n# Start a worker (operator-run, not orchestrated by this packet)\ncursor-agent worker --pool my-pool --auth-token-file ~/.cursor/worker-token\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Cursor CLI Unique Capabilities\"\ndescription: \"Cursor CLI surfaces with no sibling analog: native git worktree isolation, the cloud worker, the plugin marketplace, and MCP client support.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"cursor worktree\"\n  - \"cursor cloud worker\"\n  - \"cursor plugin marketplace\"\n  - \"cursor mcp client\"\n  - \"cursor unique surfaces\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.4.1.0\n---\n\n# Cursor CLI Unique Capabilities\n\nReference for the Cursor CLI surfaces that have **no analog** in `cli-codex`, `cli-claude-code`, or `cli-opencode`. Each is documented as an opt-in escape hatch — this packet's default dispatch (`SKILL.md` §3) never invokes any of them automatically.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nCursor CLI ships several capabilities that go beyond \"run a prompt against a model\": native git worktree isolation, a private cloud execution worker, a plugin marketplace, and Cursor's own subagent/skill system. These surfaces are documented here as deliberate, user-invoked escape hatches.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- The operator explicitly wants an experiment tried in an isolated checkout without touching the current workspace\n- The operator explicitly wants Cursor to run agents in a remote/cloud environment rather than locally\n- The operator wants to discover or manage Cursor plugins\n- A task needs an MCP server Cursor is already configured to use\n\n### Core Principle\n\nNone of these change `cli-cursor`'s `packetKind: \"workflow\"` classification (see `030-cli-cursor-creation/003-cli-cursor-skill-packet/decision-record.md` ADR-001) — the packet's default dispatch still runs locally and writes land in this repo's checkout.\n\n---\n\n## 2. NATIVE GIT WORKTREE ISOLATION\n\n### What It Is\n\n`-w` / `--worktree [name]` starts `cursor-agent` in an isolated git worktree at `~/.cursor/worktrees/<reponame>/<name>`, rather than the current working directory. `--worktree-base <branch>` sets the base ref for the new worktree. `--skip-worktree-setup` skips any setup scripts declared in `.cursor/worktrees.json`.\n\n### Why It's Out of Scope for Orchestrated Dispatch\n\nThis repo already manages its own numbered-worktree discipline via `sk-git` (owner-scoped branches, `.worktrees/{NNNN}-{owner}-{slug}` directories). A dispatched `cursor-agent` inside a deep-loop fan-out lineage already runs inside that lineage's own isolated directory — passing `-w` on top would create a SECOND, Cursor-native worktree nested inside or alongside the first, doubling isolation in a way the runtime does not expect and has not been built to reconcile. The deep-loop executor adapter (`buildCursorLineageCommand`) never passes `-w`.\n\n### When an Operator Might Use It Directly\n\n```bash\n# Try a risky refactor in a disposable worktree, leaving the current checkout untouched\ncursor-agent -p \"Attempt an aggressive refactor of the auth module\" \\\n  -w risky-refactor --model composer-2.5 --auto-review --sandbox enabled\n\n# Base the new worktree on a specific branch\ncursor-agent -p \"Prototype the new caching layer\" \\\n  -w cache-prototype --worktree-base develop --model composer-2.5\n```\n\nThis is a direct, interactive/manual operator action — not something an orchestrated fan-out or automated pipeline in this repo should invoke on its own.\n\n---\n\n## 3. CLOUD WORKER\n\n### What It Is\n\n`cursor-agent worker` runs a private cloud worker that connects to Cursor's infrastructure to run agents in the operator's own environment remotely. It is infra-grade remote execution: Kubernetes-style health probes (`GET /healthz`, `/readyz`), a Prometheus `/metrics` endpoint, pool vs. shared assignment (`--pool`/`--pool-name`), labels, and `--auth-token-file` for operator-managed secret mounts.\n\n### Why It's Out of Scope for This Packet's Runtime Wiring\n\nThis is a fundamentally different execution shape than every other capability this packet dispatches — it stands up a long-running service, not a single bounded `-p` prompt/response round-trip. Wiring it into this repo's deep-loop runtime would mean building an entirely separate execution model (service lifecycle, health checks, secret mounts) that no sibling CLI needs and that the parent packet's spec explicitly scopes out. If a future need for genuinely remote, infra-grade Cursor execution arises, that is new scope for a dedicated future packet — not a repurposing of this one's `-p` dispatch adapter.\n\n### When an Operator Might Use It Directly\n\n```bash\n# Start a worker (operator-run, not orchestrated by this packet)\ncursor-agent worker --pool my-pool --auth-token-file ~/.cursor/worker-token\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/cursor-tools.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133490532,"end":1794133491164}}}}
