{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794133642816,"sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","part":{"partID":"prt_1bab2b38d001EQAgDimvOj6axG","sessionID":"ses_e45574eb5fferLWklFUKCqoqXo","messageID":"msg_1bab2acfa001QCsvjfTKCz3MYz","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8f947e6b8e83875","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":4,\"runId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1794132897320-q8eip1\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1794132897320-q8eip1\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1794132897320-q8eip1\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Detector heuristic, false-positive surface and fixtures\",\"findingsCount\":9,\"answeredQuestions\":[\"What detector heuristic works (lettered or numbered option list plus a question near the end of the last assistant message, with no ask-tool call in the turn), and what is its false-positive risk on ordinary numbered steps, summaries and code blocks?\"],\"noveltyJustification\":\"Eight findings are new analysis of an existing detector; one is a partial synthesis of which false-positive vectors survive its prose stripper.\",\"ruledOut\":[\"Reusing isProcessQuestion as the guard filter\",\"A pure last_assistant_message check with no tool scan\"],\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.test.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/capture-core.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-transcript.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-codex.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-opencode.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-pi.mjs\",\"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-08T10:54:00Z\",\"durationMs\":600000}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-001\",\"label\":\"A question detector already exists in chat-questions.mjs: closing-paragraph question plus lettered options, with process questions skipped; the guard can reuse it.\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-002\",\"label\":\"The detector's option grammar is A-D only, so numbered, A. and Option 1: menus are invisible; enforcement needs a wider grammar.\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-003\",\"label\":\"The prose stripper removes fenced code, inline code, quotes, blockquotes, tables and headings before the question test, which is the anti-code-block defense.\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-004\",\"label\":\"Ordinary numbered steps are low risk because the option gate requires an A)-shaped marker, not a number.\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-005\",\"label\":\"Summaries are low risk while a question mark is required and no option list is printed; a summary with four A) lines is the residual intended fire.\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-006\",\"label\":\"Two false-positive vectors remain: options-only code blocks and blockquoted menus, because option extraction reads raw lines while only the question test is prose-stripped.\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-007\",\"label\":\"The no-ask-tool-call half is already implemented per runtime by the decision-capture transcript sweeps (AskUserQuestion, request_user_input, question, ask_user_question).\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-transcript.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-codex.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-opencode.mjs\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-pi.mjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-008\",\"label\":\"Claude's Stop payload carries the text but not the tool history, so the guard needs last_assistant_message plus transcript_path.\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter004-009\",\"label\":\"The fixture base is positive-only: ask fixtures exist for Claude, Codex, OpenCode, Pi and Devin plus 13 detector tests, but no negative menu fixtures.\",\"iteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/fixtures/claude-chat-questions.jsonl\",\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.test.mjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Reusing isProcessQuestion as the guard filter\",\"reason\":\"It suppresses scope, permission, gate and shipping questions from capture, which are exactly the decisions the ask surface must carry.\",\"iteration\":4}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"A pure last_assistant_message check with no tool scan\",\"reason\":\"It cannot distinguish a turn that asked through the tool from one that printed a menu.\",\"iteration\":4}\n","path":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-004.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-004.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-004.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput