sing-paragraph question plus lettered options, with process questions skipped; the guard can reuse it.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-002\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The detector's option grammar is A-D only, so numbered, A. and Option 1: menus are invisible; enforcement needs a wider grammar.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-003\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The prose stripper removes fenced code, inline code, quotes, blockquotes, tables and headings before the question test, which is the anti-code-block defense.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-004\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Ordinary numbered steps are low risk because the option gate requires an A)-shaped marker, not a number.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Summaries are low risk while a question mark is required and no option list is printed; a summary with four A) lines is the residual intended fire.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-006\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Two false-positive vectors remain: options-only code blocks and blockquoted menus, because option extraction reads raw lines while only the question test is prose-stripped.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/chat-questions.mjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-007\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The no-ask-tool-call half is already implemented p