005\",\"label\":\"The adapter layout is .skilled/hooks/<concern>/<runtime>/ with Pi and DSH real files behind symlinks in .pi/extensions and .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/README.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-006\",\"label\":\"The loop guard is stop_hook_active plus a per-turn marker; Claude caps consecutive continuations at 8, so the adapter must approve when stop_hook_active is true.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-007\",\"label\":\"The escape hatch already exists: isHookEnabled('ask-surface') resolves SYSTEM_ASK_SURFACE_DISABLED, the master SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED disables everything, and env wins over hook-flags.env.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-008\",\"label\":\"Naming a tool in AGENTS.md Gate 3 would breach the ask-surface carve-out, which makes communication-handoff.md §5 the only place a tool name may appear; Gate 3 must reference §5 instead.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"REPO RULES.md\",\".skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-009\",\"label\":\"communication-handoff.md §5 is stale for OpenCode (name not recorded; it is question) and its fallback sentence sanctions a prose numbered list for any runtime without a surface.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-010\",\"label\":\"Amendment set: §4 adds ask-through-§5, §5 updates the runtime rows and narrows the fallback to no-surface or unavailable-surface sessions, and Gate 3 references §5 while keeping A/B/C/D as option labels.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"REPO RULES.md\",\".skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md\",\"AGENTS.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"A blocking guard on every runtime\",\"reason\":\"Only Claude Code and DSH expose a turn-end seam; the rest get observe-only adapters plus rule text.\",\"iteration\":5}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Naming the tool in AGENTS.md\",\"reason\":\"It breaches the ask-surface carve-out and duplicates a table §5 already owns.\",\"iteration\":5}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Removing the prose fallback entirely\",\"reason\":\"Claude subagents, DSH headless runs and codex exec have no ask tool, so a rule with no fallback would be unsatisfiable there.\",\"iteration\":5}\n","path":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-005.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-005.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-005.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-deepseek-1794132897320-q8eip1\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-deepseek-1794132897320-q8eip1\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-deepseek-1794132897320-q8eip1\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":0.85,\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Wiring, escape hatch and rule-text amendments\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":10,\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"Per runtime: which hook or plugin event can deterministically detect a turn that ends in a prose option menu with no ask-tool call, and block or re-prompt it? Which events can only observe?\\\",\\\"How should this be wired through hook-registry.json, sync-hook-registrations.cjs and the .skilled/hooks/<name>/<runtime>/ layout, reusing the decision-capture adapters, with the loop guard, sync versus async, and the escape hatch?\\\",\\\"What exact rule-text amendments should go into communication-handoff.md §4/§5 and AGENTS.md Gate 3 inside the REPO RULES.md ask-surface carve-out, and should the prose fallback stay for runtimes without a tool?\\\"],\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"Eight findings are new wiring facts and two are a composed amendment set, with the carve-out conflict as the genuinely new constraint.\\\",\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"A blocking guard on every runtime\\\",\\\"Naming the tool in AGENTS.md\\\",\\\"Removing the prose fallback entirely\\\"],\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Grep\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/hook-registry.json\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/README.md\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs\\\",\\\".skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md\\\",\\\"REPO RULES.md\\\",\\\".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md\\\",\\\"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks\\\"],\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-08T11:04:00Z\\\",\\\"durationMs\\\":600000}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-001\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"hook-registry.json covers claude, codex, cursor, devin and Pi; DSH registers through .dsh/plugins/repo-guards and OpenCode through .opencode/plugins, so a complete guard needs three registration surfaces.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/hook-registry.json\\\",\\\".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-002\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"A new hook is one registry entry with per-runtime bindings; the synchronizer renders the four JSON files and --check reports drift, so generated files are never hand-edited.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-003\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Blocking is the absence of async: the renderer emits hook.async only when binding.async is set, and async means background without blocking.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs\\\",\\\"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-004\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The fallback field encodes per-runtime drift behaviour: Codex Stop rejects unknown hookSpecificOutput keys and takes systemMessage, while Cursor's envelope is permission:allow plus agent_message.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The adapter layout is .skilled/hooks/<concern>/<runtime>/ with Pi and DSH real files behind symlinks in .pi/extensions and .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/README.md\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-006\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The loop guard is stop_hook_active plus a per-turn marker; Claude caps consecutive continuations at 8, so the adapter must approve when stop_hook_active is true.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-007\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The escape hatch already exists: isHookEnabled('ask-surface') resolves SYSTEM_ASK_SURFACE_DISABLED, the master SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED disables everything, and env wins over hook-flags.env.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-008\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Naming a tool in AGENTS.md Gate 3 would breach the ask-surface carve-out, which makes communication-handoff.md §5 the only place a tool name may appear; Gate 3 must reference §5 instead.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"REPO RULES.md\\\",\\\".skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-009\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"communication-handoff.md §5 is stale for OpenCode (name not recorded; it is question) and its fallback sentence sanctions a prose numbered list for any runtime without a surface.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter005-010\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Amendment set: §4 adds ask-through-§5, §5 updates the runtime rows and narrows the fallback to no-surface or unavailable-surface sessions, and Gate 3 references §5 while keeping A/B/C/D as option labels.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"REPO RULES.md\\\",\\\".skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md\\\",\\\"AGENTS.md\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"A blocking guard on every runtime\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Only Claude Code and DSH expose a turn-end seam; the rest get observe-only adapters plus rule text.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Naming the tool in AGENTS.md\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"It breaches the ask-surface carve-out and duplicates a table §5 already owns.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Removing the prose fallback entirely\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Claude subagents, DSH headless runs and codex exec have no ask tool, so a rule with no fallback would be unsatisfiable there.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":5}\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/027-ask-surface-enforcement/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-005.jsonl\"}"},"time":{"start":1794133706708,"end":1794133715674}}}}
